var BIBLE_RNKJV = {
"matthew-plain":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The book of the genealogy of YahuShua HaMashiach, the Son of David, the Son of Abraham:"},{"n":16,"text":"And Jacob begot Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born YahuShua who is called Mashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations, from David until the captivity in Babylon are fourteen generations, and from the captivity in Babylon until HaMashiach are fourteen generations."},{"n":18,"text":"Now the birth of YahuShua HaMashiach was as follows: After His mother Mary was betrothed to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Spirit."},{"n":21,"text":"And she will bring forth a Son, and you shall call His name YAHUSHUA, for He will save His people from their sins.”"},{"n":25,"text":"and did not know her till she had brought forth her firstborn Son. And he called His name YAHUSHUA."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Now after YahuShua was born in Bethlehem of Judea in the days of Herod the king, behold, wise men from the East came to Jerusalem,"},{"n":4,"text":"And when he had gathered all the chief priests and scribes of the people together, he inquired of them where HaMashiach was to be born."}],"3":[{"n":13,"text":"Then YahuShua came from Galilee to John at the Jordan to be baptized by him."},{"n":15,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said to him, “Permit it to be so now, for thus it is fitting for us to fulfill all righteousness.” Then he allowed Him."},{"n":16,"text":"When He had been baptized, YahuShua came up immediately from the water; and behold, the heavens were opened to Him, and He saw the Spirit of God descending like a dove and alighting upon Him."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua was led up by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil."},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “It is written again, ‘You shall not tempt the LORD your God.’ ”"},{"n":10,"text":"Then YahuShua said to him, “Away with you, Satan! For it is written, ‘You shall worship the LORD your God, and Him only you shall serve.’ ”"},{"n":12,"text":"Now when YahuShua heard that John had been put in prison, He departed to Galilee."},{"n":17,"text":"From that time YahuShua began to preach and to say, “Repent, for the kingdom of heaven is at hand.”"},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua, walking by the Sea of Galilee, saw two brothers, Simon called Peter, and Andrew his brother, casting a net into the sea; for they were fishermen."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua went about all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing all kinds of sickness and all kinds of disease among the people."}],"7":[{"n":28,"text":"And so it was, when YahuShua had ended these sayings, that the people were astonished at His teaching,"}],"8":[{"n":3,"text":"Then YahuShua put out His hand and touched him, saying, “I am willing; be cleansed.” Immediately his leprosy was cleansed."},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “See that you tell no one; but go your way, show yourself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, as a testimony to them.”"},{"n":5,"text":"Now when YahuShua had entered Capernaum, a centurion came to Him, pleading with Him,"},{"n":7,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “I will come and heal him.”"},{"n":10,"text":"When YahuShua heard it, He marveled, and said to those who followed, “Assuredly, I say to you, I have not found such great faith, not even in Israel!"},{"n":13,"text":"Then YahuShua said to the centurion, “Go your way; and as you have believed, so let it be done for you.” And his servant was healed that same hour."},{"n":14,"text":"Now when YahuShua had come into Peter’s house, He saw his wife’s mother lying sick with a fever."},{"n":18,"text":"And when YahuShua saw great multitudes about Him, He gave a command to depart to the other side."},{"n":20,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “Foxes have holes and birds of the air have nests, but the Son of Man has nowhere to lay His head.”"},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “Follow Me, and let the dead bury their own dead.”"},{"n":29,"text":"And suddenly they cried out, saying, “What have we to do with You, YahuShua, You Son of God? Have You come here to torment us before the time?”"},{"n":34,"text":"And behold, the whole city came out to meet YahuShua. And when they saw Him, they begged Him to depart from their region."}],"9":[{"n":2,"text":"Then behold, they brought to Him a paralytic lying on a bed. When YahuShua saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, be of good cheer; your sins are forgiven you.”"},{"n":4,"text":"But YahuShua, knowing their thoughts, said, “Why do you think evil in your hearts?"},{"n":9,"text":"As YahuShua passed on from there, He saw a man named Matthew sitting at the tax office. And He said to him, “Follow Me.” So he arose and followed Him."},{"n":10,"text":"Now it happened, as YahuShua sat at the table in the house, that behold, many tax collectors and sinners came and sat down with Him and His disciples."},{"n":12,"text":"When YahuShua heard that, He said to them, “Those who are well have no need of a physician, but those who are sick."},{"n":15,"text":"And YahuShua said to them, “Can the friends of the bridegroom mourn as long as the bridegroom is with them? But the days will come when the bridegroom will be taken away from them, and then they will fast."},{"n":19,"text":"So YahuShua arose and followed him, and so did His disciples."},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua turned around, and when He saw her He said, “Be of good cheer, daughter; your faith has made you well.” And the woman was made well from that hour."},{"n":23,"text":"When YahuShua came into the ruler’s house, and saw the flute players and the noisy crowd wailing,"},{"n":27,"text":"When YahuShua departed from there, two blind men followed Him, crying out and saying, “Son of David, have mercy on us!”"},{"n":28,"text":"And when He had come into the house, the blind men came to Him. And YahuShua said to them, “Do you believe that I am able to do this?” They said to Him, “Yes, Lord.”"},{"n":30,"text":"And their eyes were opened. And YahuShua sternly warned them, saying, “See that no one knows it.”"},{"n":35,"text":"Then YahuShua went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among the people."}],"10":[{"n":5,"text":"These twelve YahuShua sent out and commanded them, saying: “Do not go into the way of the Gentiles, and do not enter a city of the Samaritans."}],"11":[{"n":1,"text":"Now it came to pass, when YahuShua finished commanding His twelve disciples, that He departed from there to teach and to preach in their cities."},{"n":2,"text":"And when John had heard in prison about the works of HaMashiach, he sent two of his disciples"},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Go and tell John the things which you hear and see:"},{"n":7,"text":"As they departed, YahuShua began to say to the multitudes concerning John: “What did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken by the wind?"},{"n":25,"text":"At that time YahuShua answered and said, “I thank You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that You have hidden these things from the wise and prudent and have revealed them to babes."}],"12":[{"n":1,"text":"At that time YahuShua went through the grainfields on the Sabbath. And His disciples were hungry, and began to pluck heads of grain and to eat."},{"n":15,"text":"But when YahuShua knew it, He withdrew from there. And great multitudes followed Him, and He healed them all."},{"n":25,"text":"But YahuShua knew their thoughts, and said to them: “Every kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation, and every city or house divided against itself will not stand."}],"13":[{"n":1,"text":"On the same day YahuShua went out of the house and sat by the sea."},{"n":34,"text":"All these things YahuShua spoke to the multitude in parables; and without a parable He did not speak to them,"},{"n":36,"text":"Then YahuShua sent the multitude away and went into the house. And His disciples came to Him, saying, “Explain to us the parable of the tares of the field.”"},{"n":51,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Have you understood all these things?” They said to Him, “Yes, Lord.”"},{"n":53,"text":"Now it came to pass, when YahuShua had finished these parables, that He departed from there."},{"n":57,"text":"So they were offended at Him. But YahuShua said to them, “A prophet is not without honor except in his own country and in his own house.”"}],"14":[{"n":1,"text":"At that time Herod the tetrarch heard the report about YahuShua"},{"n":12,"text":"Then his disciples came and took away the body and buried it, and went and told YahuShua."},{"n":13,"text":"When YahuShua heard it, He departed from there by boat to a deserted place by Himself. But when the multitudes heard it, they followed Him on foot from the cities."},{"n":14,"text":"And when YahuShua went out He saw a great multitude; and He was moved with compassion for them, and healed their sick."},{"n":16,"text":"But YahuShua said to them, “They do not need to go away. You give them something to eat.”"},{"n":22,"text":"Immediately YahuShua made His disciples get into the boat and go before Him to the other side, while He sent the multitudes away."},{"n":25,"text":"Now in the fourth watch of the night YahuShua went to them, walking on the sea."},{"n":27,"text":"But immediately YahuShua spoke to them, saying, “Be of good cheer! It is I; do not be afraid.”"},{"n":29,"text":"So He said, “Come.” And when Peter had come down out of the boat, he walked on the water to go to YahuShua."},{"n":31,"text":"And immediately YahuShua stretched out His hand and caught him, and said to him, “O you of little faith, why did you doubt?”"}],"15":[{"n":1,"text":"Then the scribes and Pharisees who were from Jerusalem came to YahuShua, saying,"},{"n":16,"text":"So YahuShua said, “Are you also still without understanding?"},{"n":21,"text":"Then YahuShua went out from there and departed to the region of Tyre and Sidon."},{"n":28,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said to her, “O woman, great is your faith! Let it be to you as you desire.” And her daughter was healed from that very hour."},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua departed from there, skirted the Sea of Galilee, and went up on the mountain and sat down there."},{"n":30,"text":"Then great multitudes came to Him, having with them the lame, blind, mute, maimed, and many others; and they laid them down at YahuShua’s feet, and He healed them."},{"n":32,"text":"Now YahuShua called His disciples to Himself and said, “I have compassion on the multitude, because they have now continued with Me three days and have nothing to eat. And I do not want to send them away hungry, lest they faint on the way.”"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “How many loaves do you have?” And they said, “Seven, and a few little fish.”"}],"16":[{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Take heed and beware of the leaven of the Pharisees and the Sadducees.”"},{"n":8,"text":"But YahuShua, being aware of it, said to them, “O you of little faith, why do you reason among yourselves because you have brought no bread?"},{"n":13,"text":"When YahuShua came into the region of Caesarea Philippi, He asked His disciples, saying, “Who do men say that I, the Son of Man, am?”"},{"n":16,"text":"Simon Peter answered and said, “You are HaMashiach, the Son of the living God.”"},{"n":17,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “Blessed are you, Simon Bar-Jonah, for flesh and blood has not revealed this to you, but My Father who is in heaven."},{"n":20,"text":"Then He commanded His disciples that they should tell no one that He was YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"From that time YahuShua began to show to His disciples that He must go to Jerusalem, and suffer many things from the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and be raised the third day."},{"n":24,"text":"Then YahuShua said to His disciples, “If anyone desires to come after Me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow Me."}],"17":[{"n":1,"text":"Now after six days YahuShua took Peter, James, and John his brother, led them up on a high mountain by themselves;"},{"n":4,"text":"Then Peter answered and said to YahuShua, “Lord, it is good for us to be here; if You wish, let us make here three tabernacles: one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.”"},{"n":7,"text":"But YahuShua came and touched them and said, “Arise, and do not be afraid.”"},{"n":8,"text":"When they had lifted up their eyes, they saw no one but YahuShua only."},{"n":9,"text":"Now as they came down from the mountain, YahuShua commanded them, saying, “Tell the vision to no one until the Son of Man is risen from the dead.”"},{"n":11,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Indeed, Elijah is coming first and will restore all things."},{"n":17,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said, “O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you? How long shall I bear with you? Bring him here to Me.”"},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua rebuked the demon, and it came out of him; and the child was cured from that very hour."},{"n":19,"text":"Then the disciples came to YahuShua privately and said, “Why could we not cast it out?”"},{"n":20,"text":"So YahuShua said to them, “Because of your unbelief; for assuredly, I say to you, if you have faith as a mustard seed, you will say to this mountain, ‘Move from here to there,’ and it will move; and nothing will be impossible for you."},{"n":22,"text":"Now while they were staying in Galilee, YahuShua said to them, “The Son of Man is about to be betrayed into the hands of men,"},{"n":25,"text":"He said, “Yes.” And when he had come into the house, YahuShua anticipated him, saying, “What do you think, Simon? From whom do the kings of the earth take customs or taxes, from their sons or from strangers?”"},{"n":26,"text":"Peter said to Him, “From strangers.” YahuShua said to him, “Then the sons are free."}],"18":[{"n":1,"text":"At that time the disciples came to YahuShua, saying, “Who then is greatest in the kingdom of heaven?”"},{"n":2,"text":"Then YahuShua called a little child to Him, set him in the midst of them,"},{"n":22,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “I do not say to you, up to seven times, but up to seventy times seven."}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"Now it came to pass, when YahuShua had finished these sayings, that He departed from Galilee and came to the region of Judea beyond the Jordan."},{"n":14,"text":"But YahuShua said, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not forbid them; for of such is the kingdom of heaven.”"},{"n":18,"text":"He said to Him, “Which ones?” YahuShua said, “‘You shall not murder,’ ‘You shall not commit adultery,’ ‘You shall not steal,’ ‘You shall not bear false witness,’"},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “If you want to be perfect, go, sell what you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow Me.”"},{"n":23,"text":"Then YahuShua said to His disciples, “Assuredly, I say to you that it is hard for a rich man to enter the kingdom of heaven."},{"n":26,"text":"But YahuShua looked at them and said to them, “With men this is impossible, but with God all things are possible.”"},{"n":28,"text":"So YahuShua said to them, “Assuredly I say to you, that in the regeneration, when the Son of Man sits on the throne of His glory, you who have followed Me will also sit on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel."}],"20":[{"n":17,"text":"Now YahuShua, going up to Jerusalem, took the twelve disciples aside on the road and said to them,"},{"n":22,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said, “You do not know what you ask. Are you able to drink the cup that I am about to drink, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?” They said to Him, “We are able.”"},{"n":25,"text":"But YahuShua called them to Himself and said, “You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them, and those who are great exercise authority over them."},{"n":30,"text":"And behold, two blind men sitting by the road, when they heard that YahuShua was passing by, cried out, saying, “Have mercy on us, O Lord, Son of David!”"},{"n":32,"text":"So YahuShua stood still and called them, and said, “What do you want Me to do for you?”"},{"n":34,"text":"So YahuShua had compassion and touched their eyes. And immediately their eyes received sight, and they followed Him."}],"21":[{"n":1,"text":"Now when they drew near Jerusalem, and came to Bethphage, at the Mount of Olives, then YahuShua sent two disciples,"},{"n":6,"text":"So the disciples went and did as YahuShua commanded them."},{"n":11,"text":"So the multitudes said, “This is YahuShua, the prophet from Nazareth of Galilee.”"},{"n":12,"text":"Then YahuShua went into the temple of God and drove out all those who bought and sold in the temple, and overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those who sold doves."},{"n":16,"text":"and said to Him, “Do You hear what these are saying?” And YahuShua said to them, “Yes. Have you never read, ‘Out of the mouth of babes and nursing infants You have perfected praise’?”"},{"n":21,"text":"So YahuShua answered and said to them, “Assuredly, I say to you, if you have faith and do not doubt, you will not only do what was done to the fig tree, but also if you say to this mountain, ‘Be removed and be cast into the sea,’ it will be done."},{"n":24,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said to them, “I also will ask you one thing, which if you tell Me, I likewise will tell you by what authority I do these things:"},{"n":27,"text":"So they answered YahuShua and said, “We do not know.” And He said to them, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things."},{"n":31,"text":"Which of the two did the will of his father?” They said to Him, “The first.” YahuShua said to them, “Assuredly, I say to you that tax collectors and harlots enter the kingdom of God before you."},{"n":42,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Have you never read in the Scriptures: ‘The stone which the builders rejected Has become the chief cornerstone. This was the LORD’s doing, And it is marvelous in our eyes’?"}],"22":[{"n":1,"text":"And YahuShua answered and spoke to them again by parables and said:"},{"n":18,"text":"But YahuShua perceived their wickedness, and said, “Why do you test Me, you hypocrites?"},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “You are mistaken, not knowing the Scriptures nor the power of God."},{"n":37,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “‘You shall love the LORD your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind.’"},{"n":41,"text":"While the Pharisees were gathered together, YahuShua asked them,"},{"n":42,"text":"saying, “What do you think about HaMashiach? Whose Son is He?” They said to Him, “The Son of David.”"}],"23":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua spoke to the multitudes and to His disciples,"},{"n":8,"text":"But you, do not be called ‘Rabbi’; for One is your Teacher, HaMashiach, and you are all brethren."},{"n":10,"text":"And do not be called teachers; for One is your Teacher, HaMashiach."}],"24":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua went out and departed from the temple, and His disciples came up to show Him the buildings of the temple."},{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua said to them, “Do you not see all these things? Assuredly, I say to you, not one stone shall be left here upon another, that shall not be thrown down.”"},{"n":4,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to them: “Take heed that no one deceives you."},{"n":5,"text":"For many will come in My name, saying, ‘I am HaMashiach,’ and will deceive many."},{"n":23,"text":"“Then if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is HaMashiach!’ or ‘There!’ do not believe it."},{"n":24,"text":"For false messiahs and false prophets will rise and show great signs and wonders to deceive, if possible, even the elect."}],"26":[{"n":1,"text":"Now it came to pass, when YahuShua had finished all these sayings, that He said to His disciples,"},{"n":4,"text":"and plotted to take YahuShua by trickery and kill Him."},{"n":6,"text":"And when YahuShua was in Bethany at the house of Simon the leper,"},{"n":10,"text":"But when YahuShua was aware of it, He said to them, “Why do you trouble the woman? For she has done a good work for Me."},{"n":17,"text":"Now on the first day of the Feast of Unleavened Bread the disciples came to YahuShua, saying to Him, “Where do You want us to prepare for You to eat the Passover?”"},{"n":19,"text":"So the disciples did as YahuShua had directed them; and they prepared the Passover."},{"n":26,"text":"And as they were eating, YahuShua took bread, blessed and broke it, and gave it to the disciples and said, “Take, eat; this is My body.”"},{"n":31,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “All of you will be made to stumble because of Me this night, for it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, And the sheep of the flock will be scattered.’"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Assuredly, I say to you that this night, before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.”"},{"n":36,"text":"Then YahuShua came with them to a place called Gethsemane, and said to the disciples, “Sit here while I go and pray over there.”"},{"n":49,"text":"Immediately he went up to YahuShua and said, “Greetings, Rabbi!” and kissed Him."},{"n":50,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “Friend, why have you come?” Then they came and laid hands on YahuShua and took Him."},{"n":51,"text":"And suddenly, one of those who were with YahuShua stretched out his hand and drew his sword, struck the servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear."},{"n":52,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “Put your sword in its place, for all who take the sword will perish by the sword."},{"n":55,"text":"In that hour YahuShua said to the multitudes, “Have you come out, as against a robber, with swords and clubs to take Me? I sat daily with you, teaching in the temple, and you did not seize Me."},{"n":57,"text":"And those who had laid hold of YahuShua led Him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were assembled."},{"n":59,"text":"Now the chief priests, the elders, and all the council sought false testimony against YahuShua to put Him to death,"},{"n":63,"text":"But YahuShua kept silent. And the high priest answered and said to Him, “I put You under oath by the living God: Tell us if You are HaMashiach, the Son of God!”"},{"n":64,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “It is as you said. Nevertheless, I say to you, hereafter you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of the Power, and coming on the clouds of heaven.”"},{"n":68,"text":"saying, “Prophesy to us, HaMashiach! Who is the one who struck You?”"},{"n":69,"text":"Now Peter sat outside in the courtyard. And a servant girl came to him, saying, “You also were with YahuShua of Galilee.”"},{"n":71,"text":"And when he had gone out to the gateway, another girl saw him and said to those who were there, “This fellow also was with YahuShua of Nazareth.”"},{"n":75,"text":"And Peter remembered the word of YahuShua who had said to him, “Before the rooster crows, you will deny Me three times.” So he went out and wept bitterly."}],"27":[{"n":1,"text":"When morning came, all the chief priests and elders of the people plotted against YahuShua to put Him to death."},{"n":11,"text":"Now YahuShua stood before the governor. And the governor asked Him, saying, “Are You the King of the Jews?” YahuShua said to him, “It is as you say.”"},{"n":17,"text":"Therefore, when they had gathered together, Pilate said to them, “Whom do you want me to release to you? Barabbas, or YahuShua who is called Mashiach?”"},{"n":20,"text":"But the chief priests and elders persuaded the multitudes that they should ask for Barabbas and destroy YahuShua."},{"n":22,"text":"Pilate said to them, “What then shall I do with YahuShua who is called Mashiach?” They all said to him, “Let Him be crucified!”"},{"n":26,"text":"Then he released Barabbas to them; and when he had scourged YahuShua, he delivered Him to be crucified."},{"n":27,"text":"Then the soldiers of the governor took YahuShua into the Praetorium and gathered the whole garrison around Him."},{"n":37,"text":"And they put up over His head the accusation written against Him: THIS IS YAHUSHUA THE KING OF THE JEWS."},{"n":46,"text":"And about the ninth hour YahuShua cried out with a loud voice, saying, “Eli, Eli, lama sabachthani?” that is, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”"},{"n":50,"text":"And YahuShua cried out again with a loud voice, and yielded up His spirit."},{"n":54,"text":"So when the centurion and those with him, who were guarding YahuShua, saw the earthquake and the things that had happened, they feared greatly, saying, “Truly this was the Son of God!”"},{"n":55,"text":"And many women who followed YahuShua from Galilee, ministering to Him, were there looking on from afar,"},{"n":57,"text":"Now when evening had come, there came a rich man from Arimathea, named Joseph, who himself had also become a disciple of YahuShua."},{"n":58,"text":"This man went to Pilate and asked for the body of YahuShua. Then Pilate commanded the body to be given to him."}],"28":[{"n":5,"text":"But the angel answered and said to the women, “Do not be afraid, for I know that you seek YahuShua who was crucified."},{"n":9,"text":"And as they went to tell His disciples, behold, YahuShua met them, saying, “Rejoice!” So they came and held Him by the feet and worshiped Him."},{"n":10,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Do not be afraid. Go and tell My brethren to go to Galilee, and there they will see Me.”"},{"n":16,"text":"Then the eleven disciples went away into Galilee, to the mountain which YahuShua had appointed for them."},{"n":18,"text":"And YahuShua came and spoke to them, saying, “All authority has been given to Me in heaven and on earth."}]},
"mark":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The beginning of the gospel of YahuShua HaMashiach, the Son of God."},{"n":9,"text":"It came to pass in those days that YahuShua came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized by John in the Jordan."},{"n":14,"text":"Now after John was put in prison, YahuShua came to Galilee, preaching the gospel of the kingdom of God,"},{"n":17,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Follow Me, and I will make you become fishers of men.”"},{"n":24,"text":"saying, “Let us alone! What have we to do with You, YahuShua of Nazareth? Did You come to destroy us? I know who You are—the Holy One of God!”"},{"n":25,"text":"But YahuShua rebuked him, saying, “Be quiet, and come out of him!”"},{"n":41,"text":"Then YahuShua, moved with compassion, stretched out His hand and touched him, and said to him, “I am willing; be cleansed.”"},{"n":45,"text":"However, he went out and began to proclaim it freely, and to spread the matter, so that YahuShua could no longer openly enter the city, but was outside in deserted places; and they came to Him from every direction."}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"When YahuShua saw their faith, He said to the paralytic, “Son, your sins are forgiven you.”"},{"n":8,"text":"But immediately, when YahuShua perceived in His spirit that they reasoned thus within themselves, He said to them, “Why do you reason about these things in your hearts?"},{"n":15,"text":"Now it happened, as He was dining in Levi’s house, that many tax collectors and sinners also sat together with YahuShua and His disciples; for there were many, and they followed Him."},{"n":17,"text":"When YahuShua heard it, He said to them, “Those who are well have no need of a physician, but those who are sick. I did not come to call the righteous, but sinners, to repentance.”"},{"n":19,"text":"And YahuShua said to them, “Can the friends of the bridegroom fast while the bridegroom is with them? As long as they have the bridegroom with them they cannot fast."}],"3":[{"n":7,"text":"But YahuShua withdrew with His disciples to the sea. And a great multitude from Galilee followed Him, and from Judea"}],"5":[{"n":6,"text":"When he saw YahuShua from afar, he ran and worshiped Him."},{"n":7,"text":"And he cried out with a loud voice and said, “What have I to do with You, YahuShua, Son of the Most High God? I implore You by God that You do not torment me.”"},{"n":13,"text":"And at once YahuShua gave them permission. Then the unclean spirits went out and entered the swine (there were about two thousand); and the herd ran violently down the steep place into the sea, and drowned in the sea."},{"n":15,"text":"Then they came to YahuShua, and saw the one who had been demon-possessed and had the legion, sitting and clothed and in his right mind. And they were afraid."},{"n":19,"text":"However, YahuShua did not permit him, but said to him, “Go home to your friends, and tell them what great things the Lord has done for you, and how He has had compassion on you.”"},{"n":20,"text":"And he departed and began to proclaim in Decapolis all that YahuShua had done for him; and all marveled."},{"n":21,"text":"Now when YahuShua had crossed over again by boat to the other side, a great multitude gathered to Him; and He was by the sea."},{"n":24,"text":"So YahuShua went with him, and a great multitude followed Him and thronged Him."},{"n":27,"text":"When she heard about YahuShua, she came behind Him in the crowd and touched His garment."},{"n":30,"text":"And YahuShua, immediately knowing in Himself that power had gone out of Him, turned around in the crowd and said, “Who touched My clothes?”"},{"n":36,"text":"As soon as YahuShua heard the word that was spoken, He said to the ruler of the synagogue, “Do not be afraid; only believe.”"}],"6":[{"n":4,"text":"But YahuShua said to them, “A prophet is not without honor except in his own country, among his own relatives, and in his own house.”"},{"n":30,"text":"Then the apostles gathered to YahuShua and told Him all things, both what they had done and what they had taught."},{"n":34,"text":"And YahuShua, when He came out, saw a great multitude and was moved with compassion for them, because they were like sheep not having a shepherd. So He began to teach them many things."}],"7":[{"n":27,"text":"But YahuShua said to her, “Let the children be filled first, for it is not good to take the children’s bread and throw it to the little dogs.”"}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"In those days, the multitude being very great and having nothing to eat, YahuShua called His disciples to Him and said to them,"},{"n":17,"text":"But YahuShua, being aware of it, said to them, “Why do you reason because you have no bread? Do you not yet perceive nor understand? Is your heart still hardened?"},{"n":27,"text":"Now YahuShua and His disciples went out to the towns of Caesarea Philippi; and on the road He asked His disciples, saying to them, “Who do men say that I am?”"},{"n":29,"text":"He said to them, “But who do you say that I am?” Peter answered and said to Him, “You are HaMashiach.”"}],"9":[{"n":2,"text":"Now after six days YahuShua took Peter, James, and John, and led them up on a high mountain apart by themselves; and He was transfigured before them."},{"n":4,"text":"And Elijah appeared to them with Moses, and they were talking with YahuShua."},{"n":5,"text":"Then Peter answered and said to YahuShua, “Rabbi, it is good for us to be here; and let us make three tabernacles: one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah”—"},{"n":8,"text":"Suddenly, when they had looked around, they saw no one anymore, but only YahuShua with themselves."},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “If you can believe, all things are possible to him who believes.”"},{"n":25,"text":"When YahuShua saw that the people came running together, He rebuked the unclean spirit, saying to it: “Deaf and dumb spirit, I command you, come out of him and enter him no more!”"},{"n":27,"text":"But YahuShua took him by the hand and lifted him up, and he arose."},{"n":39,"text":"But YahuShua said, “Do not forbid him, for no one who works a miracle in My name can soon afterward speak evil of Me."},{"n":41,"text":"For whoever gives you a cup of water to drink in My name, because you belong to HaMashiach, assuredly, I say to you, he will by no means lose his reward."}],"10":[{"n":5,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to them, “Because of the hardness of your heart he wrote you this precept."},{"n":14,"text":"But when YahuShua saw it, He was greatly displeased and said to them, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not forbid them; for of such is the kingdom of God."},{"n":18,"text":"So YahuShua said to him, “Why do you call Me good? No one is good but One, that is, God."},{"n":21,"text":"Then YahuShua, looking at him, loved him, and said to him, “One thing you lack: Go your way, sell whatever you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, take up the cross, and follow Me.”"},{"n":23,"text":"Then YahuShua looked around and said to His disciples, “How hard it is for those who have riches to enter the kingdom of God!”"},{"n":24,"text":"And the disciples were astonished at His words. But YahuShua answered again and said to them, “Children, how hard it is for those who trust in riches to enter the kingdom of God!"},{"n":27,"text":"But YahuShua looked at them and said, “With men it is impossible, but not with God; for with God all things are possible.”"},{"n":29,"text":"So YahuShua answered and said, “Assuredly, I say to you, there is no one who has left house or brothers or sisters or father or mother or wife or children or lands, for My sake and the gospel’s,"},{"n":32,"text":"Now they were on the road, going up to Jerusalem, and YahuShua was going before them; and they were amazed. And as they followed they were afraid. Then He took the twelve aside again and began to tell them the things that would happen to Him:"},{"n":38,"text":"But YahuShua said to them, “You do not know what you ask. Are you able to drink the cup that I drink, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?”"},{"n":39,"text":"They said to Him, “We are able.” So YahuShua said to them, “You will indeed drink the cup that I drink, and with the baptism I am baptized with you will be baptized;"},{"n":42,"text":"But YahuShua called them to Himself and said to them, “You know that those who are considered rulers over the Gentiles lord it over them, and their great ones exercise authority over them."},{"n":47,"text":"And when he heard that it was YahuShua of Nazareth, he began to cry out and say, “YahuShua, Son of David, have mercy on me!”"},{"n":49,"text":"So YahuShua stood still and commanded him to be called. Then they called the blind man, saying to him, “Be of good cheer. Rise, He is calling you.”"},{"n":50,"text":"And throwing aside his garment, he rose and came to YahuShua."},{"n":51,"text":"So YahuShua answered and said to him, “What do you want Me to do for you?” The blind man said to Him, “Rabboni, that I may receive my sight.”"},{"n":52,"text":"Then YahuShua said to him, “Go your way; your faith has made you well.” And immediately he received his sight and followed YahuShua on the road."}],"11":[{"n":6,"text":"And they spoke to them just as YahuShua had commanded. So they let them go."},{"n":7,"text":"Then they brought the colt to YahuShua and threw their clothes on it, and He sat on it."},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua went into Jerusalem and into the temple. So when He had looked around at all things, as the hour was already late, He went out to Bethany with the twelve."},{"n":14,"text":"In response YahuShua said to it, “Let no one eat fruit from you ever again.” And His disciples heard it."},{"n":15,"text":"So they came to Jerusalem. Then YahuShua went into the temple and began to drive out those who bought and sold in the temple, and overturned the tables of the money changers and the seats of those who sold doves."},{"n":22,"text":"So YahuShua answered and said to them, “Have faith in God."},{"n":29,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said to them, “I also will ask you one question; then answer Me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things:"},{"n":33,"text":"So they answered and said to YahuShua, “We do not know.” And YahuShua answered and said to them, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.”"}],"12":[{"n":17,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to them, “Render to Caesar the things that are Caesar’s, and to God the things that are God’s.” And they marveled at Him."},{"n":24,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Are you not therefore mistaken, because you do not know the Scriptures nor the power of God?"},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua answered him, “The first of all the commandments is: ‘Hear, O Israel, the LORD our God, the LORD is one."},{"n":34,"text":"Now when YahuShua saw that he answered wisely, He said to him, “You are not far from the kingdom of God.” But after that no one dared question Him."},{"n":35,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said, while He taught in the temple, “How is it that the scribes say that HaMashiach is the Son of David?"},{"n":41,"text":"Now YahuShua sat opposite the treasury and saw how the people put money into the treasury. And many who were rich put in much."}],"13":[{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to him, “Do you see these great buildings? Not one stone shall be left upon another, that shall not be thrown down.”"},{"n":5,"text":"And YahuShua, answering them, began to say: “Take heed that no one deceives you."},{"n":21,"text":"“Then if anyone says to you, ‘Look, here is HaMashiach!’ or, ‘Look, He is there!’ do not believe it."},{"n":22,"text":"For false messiahs and false prophets will rise and show signs and wonders to deceive, if possible, even the elect."}],"14":[{"n":6,"text":"But YahuShua said, “Let her alone. Why do you trouble her? She has done a good work for Me."},{"n":18,"text":"Now as they sat and ate, YahuShua said, “Assuredly, I say to you, one of you who eats with Me will betray Me.”"},{"n":22,"text":"And as they were eating, YahuShua took bread, blessed and broke it, and gave it to them and said, “Take, eat; this is My body.”"},{"n":27,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “All of you will be made to stumble because of Me this night, for it is written: ‘I will strike the Shepherd, And the sheep will be scattered.’"},{"n":30,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Assuredly, I say to you that today, even this night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.”"},{"n":48,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said to them, “Have you come out, as against a robber, with swords and clubs to take Me?"},{"n":53,"text":"And they led YahuShua away to the high priest; and with him were assembled all the chief priests, the elders, and the scribes."},{"n":55,"text":"Now the chief priests and all the council sought testimony against YahuShua to put Him to death, but found none."},{"n":60,"text":"And the high priest stood up in the midst and asked YahuShua, saying, “Do You answer nothing? What is it these men testify against You?”"},{"n":61,"text":"But He kept silent and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked Him, saying to Him, “Are You HaMashiach, the Son of the Blessed?”"},{"n":62,"text":"YahuShua said, “I am. And you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of the Power, and coming with the clouds of heaven.”"},{"n":67,"text":"And when she saw Peter warming himself, she looked at him and said, “You also were with YahuShua of Nazareth.”"},{"n":72,"text":"A second time the rooster crowed. Then Peter called to mind the word that YahuShua had said to him, “Before the rooster crows twice, you will deny Me three times.” And when he thought about it, he wept."}],"15":[{"n":1,"text":"Immediately, in the morning, the chief priests held a consultation with the elders and scribes and the whole council; and they bound YahuShua, led Him away, and delivered Him to Pilate."},{"n":5,"text":"But YahuShua still answered nothing, so that Pilate marveled."},{"n":15,"text":"So Pilate, wanting to gratify the crowd, released Barabbas to them; and he delivered YahuShua, after he had scourged Him, to be crucified."},{"n":32,"text":"Let HaMashiach, the King of Israel, descend now from the cross, that we may see and believe.” Even those who were crucified with Him reviled Him."},{"n":34,"text":"And at the ninth hour YahuShua cried out with a loud voice, saying, “Eloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani?” which is translated, “My God, My God, why have You forsaken Me?”"},{"n":37,"text":"And YahuShua cried out with a loud voice, and breathed His last."},{"n":43,"text":"Joseph of Arimathea, a prominent council member, who was himself waiting for the kingdom of God, coming and taking courage, went in to Pilate and asked for the body of YahuShua."}],"16":[{"n":6,"text":"But he said to them, “Do not be alarmed. You seek YahuShua of Nazareth, who was crucified. He is risen! He is not here. See the place where they laid Him."}]},
"luke":{"1":[{"n":31,"text":"And behold, you will conceive in your womb and bring forth a Son, and shall call His name YAHUSHUA."}],"2":[{"n":11,"text":"For there is born to you this day in the city of David a Savior, who is HaMashiach the Lord."},{"n":21,"text":"And when eight days were completed for the circumcision of the Child, His name was called YAHUSHUA, the name given by the angel before He was conceived in the womb."},{"n":26,"text":"And it had been revealed to him by the Holy Spirit that he would not see death before he had seen the Lord’s Mashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"So he came by the Spirit into the temple. And when the parents brought in the Child YahuShua, to do for Him according to the custom of the law,"},{"n":43,"text":"When they had finished the days, as they returned, the Boy YahuShua lingered behind in Jerusalem. And Joseph and His mother did not know it;"},{"n":52,"text":"And YahuShua increased in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and men."}],"3":[{"n":15,"text":"Now as the people were in expectation, and all reasoned in their hearts about John, whether he was HaMashiach or not,"},{"n":21,"text":"When all the people were baptized, it came to pass that YahuShua also was baptized; and while He prayed, the heaven was opened."},{"n":23,"text":"Now YahuShua Himself began His ministry at about thirty years of age, being (as was supposed) the son of Joseph, the son of Heli,"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua, being filled with the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness,"},{"n":4,"text":"But YahuShua answered him, saying, “It is written, ‘Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word of God.’ ”"},{"n":8,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to him, “Get behind Me, Satan! For it is written, ‘You shall worship the LORD your God, and Him only you shall serve.’ ”"},{"n":12,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to him, “It has been said, ‘You shall not tempt the LORD your God.’ ”"},{"n":14,"text":"Then YahuShua returned in the power of the Spirit to Galilee, and news of Him went out through all the surrounding region."},{"n":34,"text":"saying, “Let us alone! What have we to do with You, YahuShua of Nazareth? Did You come to destroy us? I know who You are— the Holy One of God!”"},{"n":35,"text":"But YahuShua rebuked him, saying, “Be quiet, and come out of him!” And when the demon had thrown him in their midst, it came out of him and did not hurt him."},{"n":41,"text":"And demons also came out of many, crying out and saying, “You are HaMashiach, the Son of God!” And He, rebuking them, did not allow them to speak, for they knew that He was HaMashiach."}],"5":[{"n":8,"text":"When Simon Peter saw it, he fell down at YahuShua’s knees, saying, “Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, O Lord!”"},{"n":10,"text":"and so also were James and John, the sons of Zebedee, who were partners with Simon. And YahuShua said to Simon, “Do not be afraid. From now on you will catch men.”"},{"n":12,"text":"And it happened when He was in a certain city, that behold, a man who was full of leprosy saw YahuShua; and he fell on his face and implored Him, saying, “Lord, if You are willing, You can make me clean.”"},{"n":19,"text":"And when they could not find how they might bring him in, because of the crowd, they went up on the housetop and let him down with his bed through the tiling into the midst before YahuShua."},{"n":22,"text":"But when YahuShua perceived their thoughts, He answered and said to them, “Why are you reasoning in your hearts?"},{"n":31,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Those who are well have no need of a physician, but those who are sick."}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"But YahuShua answering them said, “Have you not even read this, what David did when he was hungry, he and those who were with him:"},{"n":9,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “I will ask you one thing: Is it lawful on the Sabbath to do good or to do evil, to save life or to destroy?”"},{"n":11,"text":"But they were filled with rage, and discussed with one another what they might do to YahuShua."}],"7":[{"n":3,"text":"So when he heard about YahuShua, he sent elders of the Jews to Him, pleading with Him to come and heal his servant."},{"n":4,"text":"And when they came to YahuShua, they begged Him earnestly, saying that the one for whom He should do this was deserving,"},{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua went with them. And when He was already not far from the house, the centurion sent friends to Him, saying to Him, “Lord, do not trouble Yourself, for I am not worthy that You should enter under my roof."},{"n":9,"text":"When YahuShua heard these things, He marveled at him, and turned around and said to the crowd that followed Him, “I say to you, I have not found such great faith, not even in Israel!”"},{"n":19,"text":"And John, calling two of his disciples to him, sent them to YahuShua, saying, “Are You the Coming One, or do we look for another?”"},{"n":22,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Go and tell John the things you have seen and heard: that the blind see, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised, the poor have the gospel preached to them."},{"n":37,"text":"And behold, a woman in the city who was a sinner, when she knew that YahuShua sat at the table in the Pharisee’s house, brought an alabaster flask of fragrant oil,"},{"n":40,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to him, “Simon, I have something to say to you.” So he said, “Teacher, say it.”"}],"8":[{"n":28,"text":"When he saw YahuShua, he cried out, fell down before Him, and with a loud voice said, “What have I to do with You, YahuShua, Son of the Most High God? I beg You, do not torment me!”"},{"n":30,"text":"YahuShua asked him, saying, “What is your name?” And he said, “Legion,” because many demons had entered him."},{"n":35,"text":"Then they went out to see what had happened, and came to YahuShua, and found the man from whom the demons had departed, sitting at the feet of YahuShua, clothed and in his right mind. And they were afraid."},{"n":38,"text":"Now the man from whom the demons had departed begged Him that he might be with Him. But YahuShua sent him away, saying,"},{"n":39,"text":"“Return to your own house, and tell what great things God has done for you.” And he went his way and proclaimed throughout the whole city what great things YahuShua had done for him."},{"n":40,"text":"So it was, when YahuShua returned, that the multitude welcomed Him, for they were all waiting for Him."},{"n":41,"text":"And behold, there came a man named Jairus, and he was a ruler of the synagogue. And he fell down at YahuShua’s feet and begged Him to come to his house,"},{"n":45,"text":"And YahuShua said, “Who touched Me?” When all denied it, Peter and those with him said, “Master, the multitudes throng and press You, and You say, ‘Who touched Me?’ ”"},{"n":46,"text":"But YahuShua said, “Somebody touched Me, for I perceived power going out from Me.”"},{"n":50,"text":"But when YahuShua heard it, He answered him, saying, “Do not be afraid; only believe, and she will be made well.”"}],"9":[{"n":20,"text":"He said to them, “But who do you say that I am?” Peter answered and said, “HaMashiach of God.”"},{"n":33,"text":"Then it happened, as they were parting from Him, that Peter said to YahuShua, “Master, it is good for us to be here; and let us make three tabernacles: one for You, one for Moses, and one for Elijah”—not knowing what he said."},{"n":36,"text":"When the voice had ceased, YahuShua was found alone. But they kept quiet, and told no one in those days any of the things they had seen."},{"n":41,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said, “O faithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you and bear with you? Bring your son here.”"},{"n":42,"text":"And as he was still coming, the demon threw him down and convulsed him. Then YahuShua rebuked the unclean spirit, healed the child, and gave him back to his father."},{"n":43,"text":"And they were all amazed at the majesty of God. But while everyone marveled at all the things which YahuShua did, He said to His disciples,"},{"n":47,"text":"And YahuShua, perceiving the thought of their heart, took a little child and set him by Him,"},{"n":50,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “Do not forbid him, for he who is not against us is on our side.”"},{"n":58,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “Foxes have holes and birds of the air have nests, but the Son of Man has nowhere to lay His head.”"},{"n":60,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Let the dead bury their own dead, but you go and preach the kingdom of God.”"},{"n":62,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “No one, having put his hand to the plow, and looking back, is fit for the kingdom of God.”"}],"10":[{"n":21,"text":"In that hour YahuShua rejoiced in the Spirit and said, “I thank You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that You have hidden these things from the wise and prudent and revealed them to babes. Even so, Father, for so it seemed good in Your sight."},{"n":29,"text":"But he, wanting to justify himself, said to YahuShua, “And who is my neighbor?”"},{"n":30,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said: “A certain man went down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and fell among thieves, who stripped him of his clothing, wounded him, and departed, leaving him half dead."},{"n":37,"text":"And he said, “He who showed mercy on him.” Then YahuShua said to him, “Go and do likewise.”"},{"n":39,"text":"And she had a sister called Mary, who also sat at YahuShua’s feet and heard His word."},{"n":41,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to her, “Martha, Martha, you are worried and troubled about many things."}],"13":[{"n":2,"text":"And YahuShua answered and said to them, “Do you suppose that these Galileans were worse sinners than all other Galileans, because they suffered such things?"},{"n":12,"text":"But when YahuShua saw her, He called her to Him and said to her, “Woman, you are loosed from your infirmity.”"},{"n":14,"text":"But the ruler of the synagogue answered with indignation, because YahuShua had healed on the Sabbath; and he said to the crowd, “There are six days on which men ought to work; therefore come and be healed on them, and not on the Sabbath day.”"}],"14":[{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua, answering, spoke to the lawyers and Pharisees, saying, “Is it lawful to heal on the Sabbath?”"}],"17":[{"n":13,"text":"And they lifted up their voices and said, “YahuShua, Master, have mercy on us!”"},{"n":17,"text":"So YahuShua answered and said, “Were there not ten cleansed? But where are the nine?"}],"18":[{"n":16,"text":"But YahuShua called them to Him and said, “Let the little children come to Me, and do not forbid them; for of such is the kingdom of God."},{"n":19,"text":"So YahuShua said to him, “Why do you call Me good? No one is good but One, that is, God."},{"n":22,"text":"So when YahuShua heard these things, He said to him, “You still lack one thing. Sell all that you have and distribute to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow Me.”"},{"n":24,"text":"And when YahuShua saw that he became very sorrowful, He said, “How hard it is for those who have riches to enter the kingdom of God!"},{"n":37,"text":"So they told him that YahuShua of Nazareth was passing by."},{"n":38,"text":"And he cried out, saying, “YahuShua, Son of David, have mercy on me!”"},{"n":40,"text":"So YahuShua stood still and commanded him to be brought to Him. And when he had come near, He asked him,"},{"n":42,"text":"Then YahuShua said to him, “Receive your sight; your faith has made you well.”"}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"Then YahuShua entered and passed through Jericho."},{"n":3,"text":"And he sought to see who YahuShua was, but could not because of the crowd, for he was of short stature."},{"n":5,"text":"And when YahuShua came to the place, He looked up and saw him, and said to him, “Zacchaeus, make haste and come down, for today I must stay at your house.”"},{"n":9,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “Today salvation has come to this house, because he also is a son of Abraham;"},{"n":35,"text":"Then they brought him to YahuShua. And they threw their own clothes on the colt, and they set YahuShua on him."}],"20":[{"n":8,"text":"And YahuShua said to them, “Neither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.”"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “The sons of this age marry and are given in marriage."},{"n":41,"text":"And He said to them, “How can they say that HaMashiach is the Son of David?"}],"22":[{"n":47,"text":"And while He was still speaking, behold, a multitude; and he who was called Judas, one of the twelve, went before them and drew near to YahuShua to kiss Him."},{"n":48,"text":"But YahuShua said to him, “Judas, are you betraying the Son of Man with a kiss?”"},{"n":51,"text":"But YahuShua answered and said, “Permit even this.” And He touched his ear and healed him."},{"n":52,"text":"Then YahuShua said to the chief priests, captains of the temple, and the elders who had come to Him, “Have you come out, as against a robber, with swords and clubs?"},{"n":63,"text":"Now the men who held YahuShua mocked Him and beat Him."},{"n":67,"text":"“If You are HaMashiach, tell us.” But He said to them, “If I tell you, you will by no means believe."}],"23":[{"n":2,"text":"And they began to accuse Him, saying, “We found this fellow perverting the nation, and forbidding to pay taxes to Caesar, saying that He Himself is HaMashiach, a King.”"},{"n":8,"text":"Now when Herod saw YahuShua, he was exceedingly glad; for he had desired for a long time to see Him, because he had heard many things about Him, and he hoped to see some miracle done by Him."},{"n":20,"text":"Pilate, therefore, wishing to release YahuShua, again called out to them."},{"n":25,"text":"And he released to them the one they requested, who for rebellion and murder had been thrown into prison; but he delivered YahuShua to their will."},{"n":26,"text":"Now as they led Him away, they laid hold of a certain man, Simon a Cyrenian, who was coming from the country, and on him they laid the cross that he might bear it after YahuShua."},{"n":28,"text":"But YahuShua, turning to them, said, “Daughters of Jerusalem, do not weep for Me, but weep for yourselves and for your children."},{"n":34,"text":"Then YahuShua said, “Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they do.” And they divided His garments and cast lots."},{"n":35,"text":"And the people stood looking on. But even the rulers with them sneered, saying, “He saved others; let Him save Himself if He is HaMashiach, the chosen of God.”"},{"n":39,"text":"Then one of the criminals who were hanged blasphemed Him, saying, “If You are HaMashiach, save Yourself and us.”"},{"n":42,"text":"Then he said to YahuShua, “Lord, remember me when You come into Your kingdom.”"},{"n":43,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “Assuredly, I say to you, today you will be with Me in Paradise.”"},{"n":46,"text":"And when YahuShua had cried out with a loud voice, He said, “Father, ‘into Your hands I commit My spirit.’ ” Having said this, He breathed His last."},{"n":52,"text":"This man went to Pilate and asked for the body of YahuShua."}],"24":[{"n":3,"text":"Then they went in and did not find the body of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":15,"text":"So it was, while they conversed and reasoned, that YahuShua Himself drew near and went with them."},{"n":19,"text":"And He said to them, “What things?” So they said to Him, “The things concerning YahuShua of Nazareth, who was a Prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people,"},{"n":26,"text":"Ought not HaMashiach to have suffered these things and to enter into His glory?”"},{"n":36,"text":"Now as they said these things, YahuShua Himself stood in the midst of them, and said to them, “Peace to you.”"},{"n":46,"text":"Then He said to them, “Thus it is written, and thus it was necessary for HaMashiach to suffer and to rise from the dead the third day,"}]},
"john":{"1":[{"n":17,"text":"For the law was given through Moses, but grace and truth came through YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"He confessed, and did not deny, but confessed, “I am not HaMashiach.”"},{"n":25,"text":"And they asked him, saying, “Why then do you baptize if you are not HaMashiach, nor Elijah, nor the Prophet?”"},{"n":29,"text":"The next day John saw YahuShua coming toward him, and said, “Behold! The Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world!"},{"n":36,"text":"And looking at YahuShua as He walked, he said, “Behold the Lamb of God!”"},{"n":37,"text":"The two disciples heard him speak, and they followed YahuShua."},{"n":38,"text":"Then YahuShua turned, and seeing them following, said to them, “What do you seek?” They said to Him, “Rabbi” (which is to say, when translated, Teacher), “where are You staying?”"},{"n":41,"text":"He first found his own brother Simon, and said to him, “We have found the Mashiach” (which is translated, the Anointed)."},{"n":42,"text":"And he brought him to YahuShua. Now when YahuShua looked at him, He said, “You are Simon the son of Jonah. You shall be called Cephas” (which is translated, A Stone)."},{"n":43,"text":"The following day YahuShua wanted to go to Galilee, and He found Philip and said to him, “Follow Me.”"},{"n":45,"text":"Philip found Nathanael and said to him, “We have found Him of whom Moses in the law, and also the prophets, wrote—YahuShua of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.”"},{"n":47,"text":"YahuShua saw Nathanael coming toward Him, and said of him, “Behold, an Israelite indeed, in whom is no deceit!”"},{"n":48,"text":"Nathanael said to Him, “How do You know me?” YahuShua answered and said to him, “Before Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.”"},{"n":50,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “Because I said to you, ‘I saw you under the fig tree,’ do you believe? You will see greater things than these.”"}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"On the third day there was a wedding in Cana of Galilee, and the mother of YahuShua was there."},{"n":2,"text":"Now both YahuShua and His disciples were invited to the wedding."},{"n":3,"text":"And when they ran out of wine, the mother of YahuShua said to Him, “They have no wine.”"},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Woman, what does your concern have to do with Me? My hour has not yet come.”"},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Fill the waterpots with water.” And they filled them up to the brim."},{"n":11,"text":"This beginning of signs YahuShua did in Cana of Galilee, and manifested His glory; and His disciples believed in Him."},{"n":13,"text":"Now the Passover of the Jews was at hand, and YahuShua went up to Jerusalem."},{"n":19,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.”"},{"n":22,"text":"Therefore, when He had risen from the dead, His disciples remembered that He had said this to them; and they believed the Scripture and the word which YahuShua had said."},{"n":24,"text":"But YahuShua did not commit Himself to them, because He knew all men,"}],"3":[{"n":2,"text":"This man came to YahuShua by night and said to Him, “Rabbi, we know that You are a teacher come from God; for no one can do these signs that You do unless God is with him.”"},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born again, he cannot see the kingdom of God.”"},{"n":5,"text":"YahuShua answered, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless one is born of water and the Spirit, he cannot enter the kingdom of God."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “Are you the teacher of Israel, and do not know these things?"},{"n":22,"text":"After these things YahuShua and His disciples came into the land of Judea, and there He remained with them and baptized."},{"n":28,"text":"You yourselves bear me witness, that I said, ‘I am not HaMashiach,’ but, ‘I have been sent before Him.’"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore, when the Lord knew that the Pharisees had heard that YahuShua made and baptized more disciples than John"},{"n":2,"text":"(though YahuShua Himself did not baptize, but His disciples),"},{"n":6,"text":"Now Jacob’s well was there. YahuShua therefore, being wearied from His journey, sat thus by the well. It was about the sixth hour."},{"n":7,"text":"A woman of Samaria came to draw water. YahuShua said to her, “Give Me a drink.”"},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to her, “If you knew the gift of God, and who it is who says to you, ‘Give Me a drink,’ you would have asked Him, and He would have given you living water.”"},{"n":13,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to her, “Whoever drinks of this water will thirst again,"},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Go, call your husband, and come here.”"},{"n":17,"text":"The woman answered and said, “I have no husband.” YahuShua said to her, “You have well said, ‘I have no husband,’"},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Woman, believe Me, the hour is coming when you will neither on this mountain, nor in Jerusalem, worship the Father."},{"n":25,"text":"The woman said to Him, “I know that Mashiach is coming” (who is called the Anointed). “When He comes, He will tell us all things.”"},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “I who speak to you am He.”"},{"n":29,"text":"“Come, see a Man who told me all things that I ever did. Could this be HaMashiach?”"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “My food is to do the will of Him who sent Me, and to finish His work."},{"n":42,"text":"Then they said to the woman, “Now we believe, not because of what you said, for we ourselves have heard Him and we know that this is indeed HaMashiach, the Savior of the world.”"},{"n":44,"text":"For YahuShua Himself testified that a prophet has no honor in his own country."},{"n":46,"text":"So YahuShua came again to Cana of Galilee where He had made the water wine. And there was a certain nobleman whose son was sick at Capernaum."},{"n":47,"text":"When he heard that YahuShua had come out of Judea into Galilee, he went to Him and implored Him to come down and heal his son, for he was at the point of death."},{"n":48,"text":"Then YahuShua said to him, “Unless you people see signs and wonders, you will by no means believe.”"},{"n":50,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Go your way; your son lives.” So the man believed the word that YahuShua spoke to him, and he went his way."},{"n":53,"text":"So the father knew that it was at the same hour in which YahuShua said to him, “Your son lives.” And he himself believed, and his whole household."},{"n":54,"text":"This again is the second sign YahuShua did when He had come out of Judea into Galilee."}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"After this there was a feast of the Jews, and YahuShua went up to Jerusalem."},{"n":6,"text":"When YahuShua saw him lying there, and knew that he already had been in that condition a long time, He said to him, “Do you want to be made well?”"},{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Rise, take up your bed and walk.”"},{"n":13,"text":"But the one who was healed did not know who it was, for YahuShua had withdrawn, a multitude being in that place."},{"n":14,"text":"Afterward YahuShua found him in the temple, and said to him, “See, you have been made well. Sin no more, lest a worse thing come upon you.”"},{"n":15,"text":"The man departed and told the Jews that it was YahuShua who had made him well."},{"n":16,"text":"For this reason the Jews persecuted YahuShua, and sought to kill Him, because He had done these things on the Sabbath."},{"n":17,"text":"But YahuShua answered them, “My Father has been working until now, and I have been working.”"},{"n":19,"text":"Then YahuShua answered and said to them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, the Son can do nothing of Himself, but what He sees the Father do; for whatever He does, the Son also does in like manner."}],"6":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua went over the Sea of Galilee, which is the Sea of Tiberias."},{"n":3,"text":"And YahuShua went up on the mountain, and there He sat with His disciples."},{"n":5,"text":"Then YahuShua lifted up His eyes, and seeing a great multitude coming toward Him, He said to Philip, “Where shall we buy bread, that these may eat?”"},{"n":10,"text":"Then YahuShua said, “Make the people sit down.” Now there was much grass in the place. So the men sat down, in number about five thousand."},{"n":11,"text":"And YahuShua took the loaves, and when He had given thanks He distributed them to the disciples, and the disciples to those sitting down; and likewise of the fish, as much as they wanted."},{"n":14,"text":"Then those men, when they had seen the sign that YahuShua did, said, “This is truly the Prophet who is to come into the world.”"},{"n":15,"text":"Therefore when YahuShua perceived that they were about to come and take Him by force to make Him king, He departed again to the mountain by Himself alone."},{"n":17,"text":"got into the boat, and went over the sea toward Capernaum. And it was already dark, and YahuShua had not come to them."},{"n":19,"text":"So when they had rowed about three or four miles, they saw YahuShua walking on the sea and drawing near the boat; and they were afraid."},{"n":22,"text":"On the following day, when the people who were standing on the other side of the sea saw that there was no other boat there, except that one which His disciples had entered, and that YahuShua had not entered the boat with His disciples, but His disciples had gone away alone—"},{"n":24,"text":"when the people therefore saw that YahuShua was not there, nor His disciples, they also got into boats and came to Capernaum, seeking YahuShua."},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua answered them and said, “Most assuredly, I say to you, you seek Me, not because you saw the signs, but because you ate of the loaves and were filled."},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “This is the work of God, that you believe in Him whom He sent.”"},{"n":32,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, Moses did not give you the bread from heaven, but My Father gives you the true bread from heaven."},{"n":35,"text":"And YahuShua said to them, “I am the bread of life. He who comes to Me shall never hunger, and he who believes in Me shall never thirst."},{"n":42,"text":"And they said, “Is not this YahuShua, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How is it then that He says, ‘I have come down from heaven’?”"},{"n":43,"text":"YahuShua therefore answered and said to them, “Do not murmur among yourselves."},{"n":53,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, unless you eat the flesh of the Son of Man and drink His blood, you have no life in you."},{"n":61,"text":"When YahuShua knew in Himself that His disciples complained about this, He said to them, “Does this offend you?"},{"n":64,"text":"But there are some of you who do not believe.” For YahuShua knew from the beginning who they were who did not believe, and who would betray Him."},{"n":67,"text":"Then YahuShua said to the twelve, “Do you also want to go away?”"},{"n":69,"text":"Also we have come to believe and know that You are HaMashiach, the Son of the living God.”"},{"n":70,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “Did I not choose you, the twelve, and one of you is a devil?”"}],"7":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua walked in Galilee; for He did not want to walk in Judea, because the Jews sought to kill Him."},{"n":6,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “My time has not yet come, but your time is always ready."},{"n":14,"text":"Now about the middle of the feast YahuShua went up into the temple and taught."},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua answered them and said, “My doctrine is not Mine, but His who sent Me."},{"n":21,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “I did one work, and you all marvel."},{"n":26,"text":"But look! He speaks boldly, and they say nothing to Him. Do the rulers know indeed that this is truly HaMashiach?"},{"n":27,"text":"However, we know where this Man is from; but when HaMashiach comes, no one knows where He is from.”"},{"n":28,"text":"Then YahuShua cried out, as He taught in the temple, saying, “You both know Me, and you know where I am from; and I have not come of Myself, but He who sent Me is true, whom you do not know."},{"n":31,"text":"And many of the people believed in Him, and said, “When HaMashiach comes, will He do more signs than these which this Man has done?”"},{"n":33,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “I shall be with you a little while longer, and then I go to Him who sent Me."},{"n":37,"text":"On the last day, that great day of the feast, YahuShua stood and cried out, saying, “If anyone thirsts, let him come to Me and drink."},{"n":39,"text":"But this He spoke concerning the Spirit, whom those believing in Him would receive; for the Holy Spirit was not yet given, because YahuShua was not yet glorified."},{"n":41,"text":"Others said, “This is HaMashiach.” But some said, “Will HaMashiach come out of Galilee?"},{"n":42,"text":"Has not the Scripture said that HaMashiach comes from the seed of David and from the town of Bethlehem, where David was?”"},{"n":50,"text":"Nicodemus (he who came to YahuShua by night, being one of them) said to them,"}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"But YahuShua went to the Mount of Olives."},{"n":6,"text":"This they said, testing Him, that they might have something of which to accuse Him. But YahuShua stooped down and wrote on the ground with His finger, as though He did not hear."},{"n":9,"text":"Then those who heard it, being convicted by their conscience, went out one by one, beginning with the oldest even to the last. And YahuShua was left alone, and the woman standing in the midst."},{"n":10,"text":"When YahuShua had raised Himself up and saw no one but the woman, He said to her, “Woman, where are those accusers of yours? Has no one condemned you?”"},{"n":11,"text":"She said, “No one, Lord.” And YahuShua said to her, “Neither do I condemn you; go and sin no more.”"},{"n":12,"text":"Then YahuShua spoke to them again, saying, “I am the light of the world. He who follows Me shall not walk in darkness, but have the light of life.”"},{"n":14,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to them, “Even if I bear witness of Myself, My witness is true, for I know where I came from and where I am going; but you do not know where I come from and where I am going."},{"n":19,"text":"Then they said to Him, “Where is Your Father?” YahuShua answered, “You know neither Me nor My Father. If you had known Me, you would have known My Father also.”"},{"n":20,"text":"These words YahuShua spoke in the treasury, as He taught in the temple; and no one laid hands on Him, for His hour had not yet come."},{"n":21,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them again, “I am going away, and you will seek Me, and will die in your sin. Where I go you cannot come.”"},{"n":25,"text":"Then they said to Him, “Who are You?” And YahuShua said to them, “Just what I have been saying to you from the beginning."},{"n":28,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “When you lift up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am He, and that I do nothing of Myself; but as My Father taught Me, I speak these things."},{"n":31,"text":"Then YahuShua said to those Jews who believed Him, “If you abide in My word, you are My disciples indeed."},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, whoever commits sin is a slave of sin."},{"n":39,"text":"They answered and said to Him, “Abraham is our father.” YahuShua said to them, “If you were Abraham’s children, you would do the works of Abraham."},{"n":42,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “If God were your Father, you would love Me, for I proceeded forth and came from God; nor have I come of Myself, but He sent Me."},{"n":49,"text":"YahuShua answered, “I do not have a demon; but I honor My Father, and you dishonor Me."},{"n":54,"text":"YahuShua answered, “If I honor Myself, My honor is nothing. It is My Father who honors Me, of whom you say that He is your God."},{"n":58,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Most assuredly, I say to you, before Abraham was, I AM.”"},{"n":59,"text":"Then they took up stones to throw at Him; but YahuShua hid Himself and went out of the temple, going through the midst of them, and so passed by."}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"Now as YahuShua passed by, He saw a man who was blind from birth."},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua answered, “Neither this man nor his parents sinned, but that the works of God should be revealed in him."},{"n":11,"text":"He answered and said, “A Man called YahuShua made clay and anointed my eyes and said to me, ‘Go to the pool of Siloam and wash.’ So I went and washed, and I received sight.”"},{"n":14,"text":"Now it was a Sabbath when YahuShua made the clay and opened his eyes."},{"n":22,"text":"His parents said these things because they feared the Jews, for the Jews had agreed already that if anyone confessed that He was HaMashiach, he would be put out of the synagogue."},{"n":35,"text":"YahuShua heard that they had cast him out; and when He had found him, He said to him, “Do you believe in the Son of God?”"},{"n":37,"text":"And YahuShua said to him, “You have both seen Him and it is He who is talking with you.”"},{"n":39,"text":"And YahuShua said, “For judgment I have come into this world, that those who do not see may see, and that those who see may be made blind.”"},{"n":41,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “If you were blind, you would have no sin; but now you say, ‘We see.’ Therefore your sin remains."}],"10":[{"n":6,"text":"YahuShua used this illustration, but they did not understand the things which He spoke to them."},{"n":7,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them again, “Most assuredly, I say to you, I am the door of the sheep."},{"n":23,"text":"And YahuShua walked in the temple, in Solomon’s porch."},{"n":24,"text":"Then the Jews surrounded Him and said to Him, “How long do You keep us in doubt? If You are HaMashiach, tell us plainly.”"},{"n":25,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “I told you, and you do not believe. The works that I do in My Father’s name, they bear witness of Me."},{"n":32,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “Many good works I have shown you from My Father. For which of those works do you stone Me?”"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “Is it not written in your law, ‘I said, “You are gods” ’?"}],"11":[{"n":4,"text":"When YahuShua heard that, He said, “This sickness is not unto death, but for the glory of God, that the Son of God may be glorified through it.”"},{"n":5,"text":"Now YahuShua loved Martha and her sister and Lazarus."},{"n":9,"text":"YahuShua answered, “Are there not twelve hours in the day? If anyone walks in the day, he does not stumble, because he sees the light of this world."},{"n":13,"text":"However, YahuShua spoke of his death, but they thought that He was speaking about taking rest in sleep."},{"n":14,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them plainly, “Lazarus is dead."},{"n":17,"text":"So when YahuShua came, He found that he had already been in the tomb four days."},{"n":20,"text":"Now Martha, as soon as she heard that YahuShua was coming, went and met Him, but Mary was sitting in the house."},{"n":21,"text":"Now Martha said to YahuShua, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died."},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Your brother will rise again.”"},{"n":25,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “I am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in Me, though he may die, he shall live."},{"n":27,"text":"She said to Him, “Yes, Lord, I believe that You are HaMashiach, the Son of God, who is to come into the world.”"},{"n":30,"text":"Now YahuShua had not yet come into the town, but was in the place where Martha met Him."},{"n":32,"text":"Then, when Mary came where YahuShua was, and saw Him, she fell down at His feet, saying to Him, “Lord, if You had been here, my brother would not have died.”"},{"n":33,"text":"Therefore, when YahuShua saw her weeping, and the Jews who came with her weeping, He groaned in the spirit and was troubled."},{"n":35,"text":"YahuShua wept."},{"n":38,"text":"Then YahuShua, again groaning in Himself, came to the tomb. It was a cave, and a stone lay against it."},{"n":39,"text":"YahuShua said, “Take away the stone.” Martha, the sister of him who was dead, said to Him, “Lord, by this time there is a stench, for he has been dead four days.”"},{"n":40,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Did I not say to you that if you would believe you would see the glory of God?”"},{"n":41,"text":"Then they took away the stone from the place where the dead man was lying. And YahuShua lifted up His eyes and said, “Father, I thank You that You have heard Me."},{"n":44,"text":"And he who had died came out bound hand and foot with graveclothes, and his face was wrapped with a cloth. YahuShua said to them, “Loose him, and let him go.”"},{"n":45,"text":"Then many of the Jews who had come to Mary, and had seen the things YahuShua did, believed in Him."},{"n":46,"text":"But some of them went away to the Pharisees and told them the things YahuShua did."},{"n":51,"text":"Now this he did not say on his own authority; but being high priest that year he prophesied that YahuShua would die for the nation,"},{"n":54,"text":"Therefore YahuShua no longer walked openly among the Jews, but went from there into the country near the wilderness, to a city called Ephraim, and there remained with His disciples."},{"n":56,"text":"Then they sought YahuShua, and spoke among themselves as they stood in the temple, “What do you think—that He will not come to the feast?”"}],"12":[{"n":1,"text":"Then, six days before the Passover, YahuShua came to Bethany, where Lazarus was who had been dead, whom He had raised from the dead."},{"n":3,"text":"Then Mary took a pound of very costly oil of spikenard, anointed the feet of YahuShua, and wiped His feet with her hair. And the house was filled with the fragrance of the oil."},{"n":7,"text":"But YahuShua said, “Let her alone; she has kept this for the day of My burial."},{"n":9,"text":"Now a great many of the Jews knew that He was there; and they came, not for YahuShua’s sake only, but that they might also see Lazarus, whom He had raised from the dead."},{"n":11,"text":"because on account of him many of the Jews went away and believed in YahuShua."},{"n":12,"text":"The next day a great multitude that had come to the feast, when they heard that YahuShua was coming to Jerusalem,"},{"n":14,"text":"Then YahuShua, when He had found a young donkey, sat on it; as it is written:"},{"n":16,"text":"His disciples did not understand these things at first; but when YahuShua was glorified, then they remembered that these things were written about Him and that they had done these things to Him."},{"n":21,"text":"Then they came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida of Galilee, and asked him, saying, “Sir, we wish to see YahuShua.”"},{"n":22,"text":"Philip came and told Andrew, and in turn Andrew and Philip told YahuShua."},{"n":23,"text":"But YahuShua answered them, saying, “The hour has come that the Son of Man should be glorified."},{"n":30,"text":"YahuShua answered and said, “This voice did not come because of Me, but for your sake."},{"n":34,"text":"The people answered Him, “We have heard from the law that HaMashiach remains forever; and how can You say, ‘The Son of Man must be lifted up’? Who is this Son of Man?”"},{"n":35,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “A little while longer the light is with you. Walk while you have the light, lest darkness overtake you; he who walks in darkness does not know where he is going."},{"n":36,"text":"While you have the light, believe in the light, that you may become sons of light.” These things YahuShua spoke, and departed, and was hidden from them."},{"n":44,"text":"Then YahuShua cried out and said, “He who believes in Me, believes not in Me but in Him who sent Me."}],"13":[{"n":1,"text":"Now before the Feast of the Passover, when YahuShua knew that His hour had come that He should depart from this world to the Father, having loved His own who were in the world, He loved them to the end."},{"n":3,"text":"YahuShua, knowing that the Father had given all things into His hands, and that He had come from God and was going to God,"},{"n":7,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “What I am doing you do not understand now, but you will know after this.”"},{"n":8,"text":"Peter said to Him, “You shall never wash my feet!” YahuShua answered him, “If I do not wash you, you have no part with Me.”"},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “He who is bathed needs only to wash his feet, but is completely clean; and you are clean, but not all of you.”"},{"n":21,"text":"When YahuShua had said these things, He was troubled in spirit, and testified and said, “Most assuredly, I say to you, one of you will betray Me.”"},{"n":23,"text":"Now there was leaning on YahuShua’s bosom one of His disciples, whom YahuShua loved."},{"n":25,"text":"Then, leaning back on YahuShua’s breast, he said to Him, “Lord, who is it?”"},{"n":26,"text":"YahuShua answered, “It is he to whom I shall give a piece of bread when I have dipped it.” And having dipped the bread, He gave it to Judas Iscariot, the son of Simon."},{"n":27,"text":"Now after the piece of bread, Satan entered him. Then YahuShua said to him, “What you do, do quickly.”"},{"n":29,"text":"For some thought, because Judas had the money box, that YahuShua had said to him, “Buy those things we need for the feast,” or that he should give something to the poor."},{"n":31,"text":"So, when he had gone out, YahuShua said, “Now the Son of Man is glorified, and God is glorified in Him."},{"n":36,"text":"Simon Peter said to Him, “Lord, where are You going?” YahuShua answered him, “Where I am going you cannot follow Me now, but you shall follow Me afterward.”"},{"n":38,"text":"YahuShua answered him, “Will you lay down your life for My sake? Most assuredly, I say to you, the rooster shall not crow till you have denied Me three times."}],"14":[{"n":6,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me."},{"n":9,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Have I been with you so long, and yet you have not known Me, Philip? He who has seen Me has seen the Father; so how can you say, ‘Show us the Father’?"},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua answered and said to him, “If anyone loves Me, he will keep My word; and My Father will love him, and We will come to him and make Our home with him."}],"16":[{"n":19,"text":"Now YahuShua knew that they desired to ask Him, and He said to them, “Are you inquiring among yourselves about what I said, ‘A little while, and you will not see Me; and again a little while, and you will see Me’?"},{"n":31,"text":"YahuShua answered them, “Do you now believe?"}],"17":[{"n":1,"text":"YahuShua spoke these words, lifted up His eyes to heaven, and said: “Father, the hour has come. Glorify Your Son, that Your Son also may glorify You,"},{"n":3,"text":"And this is eternal life, that they may know You, the only true God, and YahuShua HaMashiach whom You have sent."}],"18":[{"n":1,"text":"When YahuShua had spoken these words, He went out with His disciples over the Brook Kidron, where there was a garden, which He and His disciples entered."},{"n":2,"text":"And Judas, who betrayed Him, also knew the place; for YahuShua often met there with His disciples."},{"n":4,"text":"YahuShua therefore, knowing all things that would come upon Him, went forward and said to them, “Whom are you seeking?”"},{"n":5,"text":"They answered Him, “YahuShua of Nazareth.” YahuShua said to them, “I am He.” And Judas, who betrayed Him, also stood with them."},{"n":7,"text":"Then He asked them again, “Whom are you seeking?” And they said, “YahuShua of Nazareth.”"},{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua answered, “I have told you that I am He. Therefore, if you seek Me, let these go their way,”"},{"n":11,"text":"So YahuShua said to Peter, “Put your sword into the sheath. Shall I not drink the cup which My Father has given Me?”"},{"n":12,"text":"Then the detachment of troops and the captain and the officers of the Jews arrested YahuShua and bound Him."},{"n":15,"text":"And Simon Peter followed YahuShua, and so did another disciple. Now that disciple was known to the high priest, and went with YahuShua into the courtyard of the high priest."},{"n":19,"text":"The high priest then asked YahuShua about His disciples and His doctrine."},{"n":20,"text":"YahuShua answered him, “I spoke openly to the world. I always taught in synagogues and in the temple, where the Jews always meet, and in secret I have said nothing."},{"n":22,"text":"And when He had said these things, one of the officers who stood by struck YahuShua with the palm of his hand, saying, “Do You answer the high priest like that?”"},{"n":23,"text":"YahuShua answered him, “If I have spoken evil, bear witness of the evil; but if well, why do you strike Me?”"},{"n":28,"text":"Then they led YahuShua from Caiaphas to the Praetorium, and it was early morning. But they themselves did not go into the Praetorium, lest they should be defiled, but that they might eat the Passover."},{"n":32,"text":"that the saying of YahuShua might be fulfilled which He spoke, signifying by what death He would die."},{"n":33,"text":"Then Pilate entered the Praetorium again, called YahuShua, and said to Him, “Are You the King of the Jews?”"},{"n":34,"text":"YahuShua answered him, “Are you speaking for yourself about this, or did others tell you this concerning Me?”"},{"n":36,"text":"YahuShua answered, “My kingdom is not of this world. If My kingdom were of this world, My servants would fight, so that I should not be delivered to the Jews; but now My kingdom is not from here.”"},{"n":37,"text":"Pilate therefore said to Him, “Are You a king then?” YahuShua answered, “You say rightly that I am a king. For this cause I was born, and for this cause I have come into the world, that I should bear witness to the truth. Everyone who is of the truth hears My voice.”"}],"19":[{"n":1,"text":"So then Pilate took YahuShua and scourged Him."},{"n":5,"text":"Then YahuShua came out, wearing the crown of thorns and the purple robe. And Pilate said to them, “Behold the Man!”"},{"n":9,"text":"and went again into the Praetorium, and said to YahuShua, “Where are You from?” But YahuShua gave him no answer."},{"n":11,"text":"YahuShua answered, “You could have no power at all against Me unless it had been given you from above. Therefore the one who delivered Me to you has the greater sin.”"},{"n":13,"text":"When Pilate therefore heard that saying, he brought YahuShua out and sat down in the judgment seat in a place that is called The Pavement, but in Hebrew, Gabbatha."},{"n":16,"text":"Then he delivered Him to them to be crucified. So they took YahuShua and led Him away."},{"n":18,"text":"where they crucified Him, and two others with Him, one on either side, and YahuShua in the center."},{"n":19,"text":"Now Pilate wrote a title and put it on the cross. And the writing was: YAHUSHUA OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS."},{"n":20,"text":"Then many of the Jews read this title, for the place where YahuShua was crucified was near the city; and it was written in Hebrew, Greek, and Latin."},{"n":23,"text":"Then the soldiers, when they had crucified YahuShua, took His garments and made four parts, to each soldier a part, and also the tunic. Now the tunic was without seam, woven from the top in one piece."},{"n":25,"text":"Now there stood by the cross of YahuShua His mother, and His mother’s sister, Mary the wife of Clopas, and Mary Magdalene."},{"n":26,"text":"When YahuShua therefore saw His mother, and the disciple whom He loved standing by, He said to His mother, “Woman, behold your son!”"},{"n":28,"text":"After this, YahuShua, knowing that all things were now accomplished, that the Scripture might be fulfilled, said, “I thirst!”"},{"n":30,"text":"So when YahuShua had received the sour wine, He said, “It is finished!” And bowing His head, He gave up His spirit."},{"n":33,"text":"But when they came to YahuShua and saw that He was already dead, they did not break His legs."},{"n":38,"text":"After this, Joseph of Arimathea, being a disciple of YahuShua, but secretly, for fear of the Jews, asked Pilate that he might take away the body of YahuShua; and Pilate gave him permission. So he came and took the body of YahuShua."},{"n":39,"text":"And Nicodemus, who at first came to YahuShua by night, also came, bringing a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about a hundred pounds."},{"n":40,"text":"Then they took the body of YahuShua, and bound it in strips of linen with the spices, as the custom of the Jews is to bury."},{"n":42,"text":"So there they laid YahuShua, because of the Jews’ Preparation Day, for the tomb was nearby."}],"20":[{"n":2,"text":"Then she ran and came to Simon Peter, and to the other disciple, whom YahuShua loved, and said to them, “They have taken away the Lord out of the tomb, and we do not know where they have laid Him.”"},{"n":12,"text":"And she saw two angels in white sitting, one at the head and the other at the feet, where the body of YahuShua had lain."},{"n":14,"text":"Now when she had said this, she turned around and saw YahuShua standing there, and did not know that it was YahuShua."},{"n":15,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Woman, why are you weeping? Whom are you seeking?” She, supposing Him to be the gardener, said to Him, “Sir, if You have carried Him away, tell me where You have laid Him, and I will take Him away.”"},{"n":16,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Mary!” She turned and said to Him, “Rabboni!” (which is to say, Teacher)."},{"n":17,"text":"YahuShua said to her, “Do not cling to Me, for I have not yet ascended to My Father; but go to My brethren and say to them, ‘I am ascending to My Father and your Father, and to My God and your God.’ ”"},{"n":19,"text":"Then, the same day at evening, being the first day of the week, when the doors were shut where the disciples were assembled, for fear of the Jews, YahuShua came and stood in the midst, and said to them, “Peace be with you.”"},{"n":21,"text":"So YahuShua said to them again, “Peace to you! As the Father has sent Me, I also send you.”"},{"n":24,"text":"Now Thomas, called the Twin, one of the twelve, was not with them when YahuShua came."},{"n":26,"text":"And after eight days His disciples were again inside, and Thomas with them. YahuShua came, the doors being shut, and stood in the midst, and said, “Peace to you!”"},{"n":29,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “Thomas, because you have seen Me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not seen and yet have believed.”"},{"n":30,"text":"And truly YahuShua did many other signs in the presence of His disciples, which are not written in this book;"},{"n":31,"text":"but these are written that you may believe that YahuShua is HaMashiach, the Son of God, and that believing you may have life in His name."}],"21":[{"n":1,"text":"After these things YahuShua showed Himself again to the disciples at the Sea of Tiberias, and in this way He showed Himself:"},{"n":4,"text":"But when the morning had now come, YahuShua stood on the shore; yet the disciples did not know that it was YahuShua."},{"n":5,"text":"Then YahuShua said to them, “Children, have you any food?” They answered Him, “No.”"},{"n":7,"text":"Therefore that disciple whom YahuShua loved said to Peter, “It is the Lord!” Now when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he put on his outer garment (for he had removed it), and plunged into the sea."},{"n":10,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Bring some of the fish which you have just caught.”"},{"n":12,"text":"YahuShua said to them, “Come and eat breakfast.” Yet none of the disciples dared ask Him, “Who are You?”—knowing that it was the Lord."},{"n":13,"text":"YahuShua then came and took the bread and gave it to them, and likewise the fish."},{"n":14,"text":"This is now the third time YahuShua showed Himself to His disciples after He was raised from the dead."},{"n":15,"text":"So when they had eaten breakfast, YahuShua said to Simon Peter, “Simon, son of Jonah, do you love Me more than these?” He said to Him, “Yes, Lord; You know that I love You.” He said to him, “Feed My lambs.”"},{"n":17,"text":"He said to him the third time, “Simon, son of Jonah, do you love Me?” Peter was grieved because He said to him the third time, “Do you love Me?” And he said to Him, “Lord, You know all things; You know that I love You.” YahuShua said to him, “Feed My sheep."},{"n":20,"text":"Then Peter, turning around, saw the disciple whom YahuShua loved following, who also had leaned on His breast at the supper, and said, “Lord, who is the one who betrays You?”"},{"n":21,"text":"Peter, seeing him, said to YahuShua, “But Lord, what about this man?”"},{"n":22,"text":"YahuShua said to him, “If I will that he remain till I come, what is that to you? You follow Me.”"},{"n":23,"text":"Then this saying went out among the brethren that this disciple would not die. Yet YahuShua did not say to him that he would not die, but, “If I will that he remain till I come, what is that to you?”"},{"n":25,"text":"And there are also many other things that YahuShua did, which if they were written one by one, I suppose that even the world itself could not contain the books that would be written. Amen."}]},
"acts":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The former account I made, O Theophilus, of all that YahuShua began both to do and teach,"},{"n":11,"text":"who also said, “Men of Galilee, why do you stand gazing up into heaven? This same YahuShua, who was taken up from you into heaven, will so come in like manner as you saw Him go into heaven.”"},{"n":14,"text":"These all continued with one accord in prayer and supplication, with the women and Mary the mother of YahuShua, and with His brothers."},{"n":16,"text":"“Men and brethren, this Scripture had to be fulfilled, which the Holy Spirit spoke before by the mouth of David concerning Judas, who became a guide to those who arrested YahuShua;"},{"n":21,"text":"“Therefore, of these men who have accompanied us all the time that the Lord YahuShua went in and out among us,"}],"2":[{"n":22,"text":"“Men of Israel, hear these words: YahuShua of Nazareth, a Man attested by God to you by miracles, wonders, and signs which God did through Him in your midst, as you yourselves also know—"},{"n":30,"text":"Therefore, being a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him that of the fruit of his body, according to the flesh, He would raise up HaMashiach to sit on his throne,"},{"n":31,"text":"he, foreseeing this, spoke concerning the resurrection of HaMashiach, that His soul was not left in Hades, nor did His flesh see corruption."},{"n":32,"text":"This YahuShua God has raised up, of which we are all witnesses."},{"n":36,"text":"“Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly that God has made this YahuShua, whom you crucified, both Lord and Mashiach.”"},{"n":38,"text":"Then Peter said to them, “Repent, and let every one of you be baptized in the name of YahuShua HaMashiach for the remission of sins; and you shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit."}],"3":[{"n":6,"text":"Then Peter said, “Silver and gold I do not have, but what I do have I give you: In the name of YahuShua HaMashiach of Nazareth, rise up and walk.”"},{"n":13,"text":"The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, glorified His Servant YahuShua, whom you delivered up and denied in the presence of Pilate, when he was determined to let Him go."},{"n":18,"text":"But those things which God foretold by the mouth of all His prophets, that HaMashiach would suffer, He has thus fulfilled."},{"n":20,"text":"and that He may send YahuShua HaMashiach, who was preached to you before,"},{"n":26,"text":"To you first, God, having raised up His Servant YahuShua, sent Him to bless you, in turning away every one of you from your iniquities.”"}],"4":[{"n":2,"text":"being greatly disturbed that they taught the people and preached in YahuShua the resurrection from the dead."},{"n":10,"text":"let it be known to you all, and to all the people of Israel, that by the name of YahuShua HaMashiach of Nazareth, whom you crucified, whom God raised from the dead, by Him this man stands here before you whole."},{"n":13,"text":"Now when they saw the boldness of Peter and John, and perceived that they were uneducated and untrained men, they marveled. And they realized that they had been with YahuShua."},{"n":18,"text":"So they called them and commanded them not to speak at all nor teach in the name of YahuShua."},{"n":26,"text":"The kings of the earth took their stand, And the rulers were gathered together Against the LORD and against His Mashiach.’"},{"n":27,"text":"“For truly against Your holy Servant YahuShua, whom You anointed, both Herod and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles and the people of Israel, were gathered together"},{"n":30,"text":"by stretching out Your hand to heal, and that signs and wonders may be done through the name of Your holy Servant YahuShua.”"},{"n":33,"text":"And with great power the apostles gave witness to the resurrection of the Lord YahuShua. And great grace was upon them all."}],"5":[{"n":30,"text":"The God of our fathers raised up YahuShua whom you murdered by hanging on a tree."},{"n":40,"text":"And they agreed with him, and when they had called for the apostles and beaten them, they commanded that they should not speak in the name of YahuShua, and let them go."},{"n":42,"text":"And daily in the temple, and in every house, they did not cease teaching and preaching YahuShua as HaMashiach."}],"6":[{"n":14,"text":"for we have heard him say that this YahuShua of Nazareth will destroy this place and change the customs which Moses delivered to us.”"}],"7":[{"n":55,"text":"But he, being full of the Holy Spirit, gazed into heaven and saw the glory of God, and YahuShua standing at the right hand of God,"},{"n":59,"text":"And they stoned Stephen as he was calling on God and saying, “Lord YahuShua, receive my spirit.”"}],"8":[{"n":5,"text":"Then Philip went down to the city of Samaria and preached HaMashiach to them."},{"n":12,"text":"But when they believed Philip as he preached the things concerning the kingdom of God and the name of YahuShua HaMashiach, both men and women were baptized."},{"n":16,"text":"For as yet He had fallen upon none of them. They had only been baptized in the name of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":35,"text":"Then Philip opened his mouth, and beginning at this Scripture, preached YahuShua to him."},{"n":37,"text":"Then Philip said, “If you believe with all your heart, you may.” And he answered and said, “I believe that YahuShua HaMashiach is the Son of God.”"}],"9":[{"n":5,"text":"And he said, “Who are You, Lord?” Then the Lord said, “I am YahuShua, whom you are persecuting. It is hard for you to kick against the goads.”"},{"n":17,"text":"And Ananias went his way and entered the house; and laying his hands on him he said, “Brother Saul, the Lord YahuShua, who appeared to you on the road as you came, has sent me that you may receive your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.”"},{"n":20,"text":"Immediately he preached HaMashiach in the synagogues, that He is the Son of God."},{"n":22,"text":"But Saul increased all the more in strength, and confounded the Jews who dwelt in Damascus, proving that this YahuShua is HaMashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"But Barnabas took him and brought him to the apostles. And he declared to them how he had seen the Lord on the road, and that He had spoken to him, and how he had preached boldly at Damascus in the name of YahuShua."},{"n":29,"text":"And he spoke boldly in the name of the Lord YahuShua and disputed against the Hellenists, but they attempted to kill him."},{"n":34,"text":"And Peter said to him, “Aeneas, YahuShua HaMashiach heals you. Arise and make your bed.” Then he arose immediately."}],"10":[{"n":36,"text":"The word which God sent to the children of Israel, preaching peace through YahuShua HaMashiach— He is Lord of all—"},{"n":38,"text":"how God anointed YahuShua of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, who went about doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, for God was with Him."}],"11":[{"n":17,"text":"If therefore God gave them the same gift as He gave us when we believed on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who was I that I could withstand God?”"},{"n":20,"text":"But some of them were men from Cyprus and Cyrene, who, when they had come to Antioch, spoke to the Hellenists, preaching the Lord YahuShua."}],"13":[{"n":23,"text":"From this man’s seed, according to the promise, God raised up for Israel a Savior—YahuShua—"},{"n":33,"text":"God has fulfilled this for us their children, in that He has raised up YahuShua. As it is also written in the second Psalm: ‘You are My Son, Today I have begotten You.’"}],"15":[{"n":11,"text":"But we believe that through the grace of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach we shall be saved in the same manner as they.”"},{"n":26,"text":"men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"16":[{"n":18,"text":"And this she did for many days. But Paul, greatly annoyed, turned and said to the spirit, “I command you in the name of YahuShua HaMashiach to come out of her.” And he came out that very hour."},{"n":31,"text":"So they said, “Believe on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and you will be saved, you and your household.”"}],"17":[{"n":3,"text":"explaining and demonstrating that HaMashiach had to suffer and rise again from the dead, and saying, “This YahuShua whom I preach to you is HaMashiach.”"},{"n":7,"text":"Jason has harbored them, and these are all acting contrary to the decrees of Caesar, saying there is another king—YahuShua.”"},{"n":18,"text":"Then certain Epicurean and Stoic philosophers encountered him. And some said, “What does this babbler want to say?” Others said, “He seems to be a proclaimer of foreign gods,” because he preached to them YahuShua and the resurrection."}],"18":[{"n":5,"text":"When Silas and Timothy had come from Macedonia, Paul was compelled by the Spirit, and testified to the Jews that YahuShua is HaMashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"for he vigorously refuted the Jews publicly, showing from the Scriptures that YahuShua is HaMashiach."}],"19":[{"n":4,"text":"Then Paul said, “John indeed baptized with a baptism of repentance, saying to the people that they should believe on Him who would come after him, that is, on YahuShua HaMashiach.”"},{"n":5,"text":"When they heard this, they were baptized in the name of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":10,"text":"And this continued for two years, so that all who dwelt in Asia heard the word of the Lord YahuShua, both Jews and Greeks."},{"n":13,"text":"Then some of the itinerant Jewish exorcists took it upon themselves to call the name of the Lord YahuShua over those who had evil spirits, saying, “We exorcise you by the YahuShua whom Paul preaches.”"},{"n":15,"text":"And the evil spirit answered and said, “YahuShua I know, and Paul I know; but who are you?”"},{"n":17,"text":"This became known both to all Jews and Greeks dwelling in Ephesus; and fear fell on them all, and the name of the Lord YahuShua was magnified."}],"20":[{"n":21,"text":"testifying to Jews, and also to Greeks, repentance toward God and faith toward our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":24,"text":"But none of these things move me; nor do I count my life dear to myself, so that I may finish my race with joy, and the ministry which I received from the Lord YahuShua, to testify to the gospel of the grace of God."},{"n":35,"text":"I have shown you in every way, by laboring like this, that you must support the weak. And remember the words of the Lord YahuShua, that He said, ‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’ ”"}],"21":[{"n":13,"text":"Then Paul answered, “What do you mean by weeping and breaking my heart? For I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord YahuShua.”"}],"22":[{"n":8,"text":"So I answered, ‘Who are You, Lord?’ And He said to me, ‘I am YahuShua of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting.’"}],"24":[{"n":24,"text":"And after some days, when Felix came with his wife Drusilla, who was Jewish, he sent for Paul and heard him concerning the faith in HaMashiach."}],"25":[{"n":19,"text":"but had some questions against him about their own religion and about a certain YahuShua, who had died, whom Paul affirmed to be alive."}],"26":[{"n":9,"text":"“Indeed, I myself thought I must do many things contrary to the name of YahuShua of Nazareth."},{"n":15,"text":"So I said, ‘Who are You, Lord?’ And He said, ‘I am YahuShua, whom you are persecuting."},{"n":23,"text":"that HaMashiach would suffer, that He would be the first to rise from the dead, and would proclaim light to the Jewish people and to the Gentiles.”"}],"28":[{"n":23,"text":"So when they had appointed him a day, many came to him at his lodging, to whom he explained and solemnly testified of the kingdom of God, persuading them concerning YahuShua from both the Law of Moses and the Prophets, from morning till evening."},{"n":31,"text":"preaching the kingdom of God and teaching the things which concern the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach with all confidence, no one forbidding him."}]},
"romans":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a bondservant of YahuShua HaMashiach, called to be an apostle, separated to the gospel of God"},{"n":3,"text":"concerning His Son YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, who was born of the seed of David according to the flesh,"},{"n":6,"text":"among whom you also are the called of YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":7,"text":"To all who are in Rome, beloved of God, called to be saints: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"First, I thank my God through YahuShua HaMashiach for you all, that your faith is spoken of throughout the whole world."},{"n":16,"text":"For I am not ashamed of the gospel of HaMashiach, for it is the power of God to salvation for everyone who believes, for the Jew first and also for the Greek."}],"2":[{"n":16,"text":"in the day when God will judge the secrets of men by YahuShua HaMashiach, according to my gospel."}],"3":[{"n":22,"text":"even the righteousness of God, through faith in YahuShua HaMashiach, to all and on all who believe. For there is no difference;"},{"n":24,"text":"being justified freely by His grace through the redemption that is in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":26,"text":"to demonstrate at the present time His righteousness, that He might be just and the justifier of the one who has faith in YahuShua."}],"4":[{"n":24,"text":"but also for us. It shall be imputed to us who believe in Him who raised up YahuShua our Lord from the dead,"}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore, having been justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"For when we were still without strength, in due time HaMashiach died for the ungodly."},{"n":8,"text":"But God demonstrates His own love toward us, in that while we were still sinners, HaMashiach died for us."},{"n":11,"text":"And not only that, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, through whom we have now received the reconciliation."},{"n":15,"text":"But the free gift is not like the offense. For if by the one man’s offense many died, much more the grace of God and the gift by the grace of the one Man, YahuShua HaMashiach, abounded to many."},{"n":17,"text":"For if by the one man’s offense death reigned through the one, much more those who receive abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness will reign in life through the One, YahuShua HaMashiach.)"},{"n":21,"text":"so that as sin reigned in death, even so grace might reign through righteousness to eternal life through YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"Or do you not know that as many of us as were baptized into YahuShua HaMashiach were baptized into His death?"},{"n":4,"text":"Therefore we were buried with Him through baptism into death, that just as HaMashiach was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life."},{"n":8,"text":"Now if we died with HaMashiach, we believe that we shall also live with Him,"},{"n":9,"text":"knowing that HaMashiach, having been raised from the dead, dies no more. Death no longer has dominion over Him."},{"n":11,"text":"Likewise you also, reckon yourselves to be dead indeed to sin, but alive to God in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":23,"text":"For the wages of sin is death, but the gift of God is eternal life in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."}],"7":[{"n":4,"text":"Therefore, my brethren, you also have become dead to the law through the body of HaMashiach, that you may be married to another—to Him who was raised from the dead, that we should bear fruit to God."},{"n":25,"text":"I thank God—through YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord! So then, with the mind I myself serve the law of God, but with the flesh the law of sin."}],"8":[{"n":1,"text":"There is therefore now no condemnation to those who are in YahuShua HaMashiach, who do not walk according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit."},{"n":2,"text":"For the law of the Spirit of life in YahuShua HaMashiach has made me free from the law of sin and death."},{"n":9,"text":"But you are not in the flesh but in the Spirit, if indeed the Spirit of God dwells in you. Now if anyone does not have the Spirit of HaMashiach, he is not His."},{"n":10,"text":"And if HaMashiach is in you, the body is dead because of sin, but the Spirit is life because of righteousness."},{"n":11,"text":"But if the Spirit of Him who raised YahuShua from the dead dwells in you, He who raised HaMashiach from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through His Spirit who dwells in you."},{"n":17,"text":"and if children, then heirs—heirs of God and joint heirs with HaMashiach, if indeed we suffer with Him, that we may also be glorified together."},{"n":34,"text":"Who is he who condemns? It is HaMashiach who died, and furthermore is also risen, who is even at the right hand of God, who also makes intercession for us."},{"n":35,"text":"Who shall separate us from the love of HaMashiach? Shall tribulation, or distress, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword?"},{"n":39,"text":"nor height nor depth, nor any other created thing, shall be able to separate us from the love of God which is in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"I tell the truth in HaMashiach, I am not lying, my conscience also bearing me witness in the Holy Spirit,"},{"n":3,"text":"For I could wish that I myself were accursed from HaMashiach for my brethren, my countrymen according to the flesh,"},{"n":5,"text":"of whom are the fathers and from whom, according to the flesh, HaMashiach came, who is over all, the eternally blessed God. Amen."}],"10":[{"n":4,"text":"For HaMashiach is the end of the law for righteousness to everyone who believes."},{"n":6,"text":"But the righteousness of faith speaks in this way, “Do not say in your heart, ‘Who will ascend into heaven?’ ” (that is, to bring HaMashiach down from above)"},{"n":7,"text":"or, “ ‘Who will descend into the abyss?’ ” (that is, to bring HaMashiach up from the dead)."},{"n":9,"text":"that if you confess with your mouth the Lord YahuShua and believe in your heart that God has raised Him from the dead, you will be saved."}],"12":[{"n":5,"text":"so we, being many, are one body in HaMashiach, and individually members of one another."}],"13":[{"n":14,"text":"But put on the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and make no provision for the flesh, to fulfill its lusts."}],"14":[{"n":9,"text":"For to this end HaMashiach died and rose and lived again, that He might be Lord of both the dead and the living."},{"n":10,"text":"But why do you judge your brother? Or why do you show contempt for your brother? For we shall all stand before the judgment seat of HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"I know and am convinced by the Lord YahuShua that there is nothing unclean of itself; but to him who considers anything to be unclean, to him it is unclean."},{"n":15,"text":"Yet if your brother is grieved because of your food, you are no longer walking in love. Do not destroy with your food the one for whom HaMashiach died."},{"n":18,"text":"For he who serves HaMashiach in these things is acceptable to God and approved by men."}],"15":[{"n":3,"text":"For even HaMashiach did not please Himself; but as it is written, “The reproaches of those who reproached You fell on Me.”"},{"n":5,"text":"Now may the God of patience and comfort grant you to be like-minded toward one another, according to YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"that you may with one mind and one mouth glorify the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"Therefore receive one another, just as HaMashiach also received us, to the glory of God."},{"n":8,"text":"Now I say that YahuShua HaMashiach has become a servant to the circumcision for the truth of God, to confirm the promises made to the fathers,"},{"n":16,"text":"that I might be a minister of YahuShua HaMashiach to the Gentiles, ministering the gospel of God, that the offering of the Gentiles might be acceptable, sanctified by the Holy Spirit."},{"n":17,"text":"Therefore I have reason to glory in YahuShua HaMashiach in the things which pertain to God."},{"n":18,"text":"For I will not dare to speak of any of those things which HaMashiach has not accomplished through me, in word and deed, to make the Gentiles obedient—"},{"n":19,"text":"in mighty signs and wonders, by the power of the Spirit of God, so that from Jerusalem and round about to Illyricum I have fully preached the gospel of HaMashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"And so I have made it my aim to preach the gospel, not where HaMashiach was named, lest I should build on another man’s foundation,"},{"n":29,"text":"But I know that when I come to you, I shall come in the fullness of the blessing of the gospel of HaMashiach."},{"n":30,"text":"Now I beg you, brethren, through the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and through the love of the Spirit, that you strive together with me in prayers to God for me,"}],"16":[{"n":3,"text":"Greet Priscilla and Aquila, my fellow workers in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":5,"text":"Likewise greet the church that is in their house. Greet my beloved Epaenetus, who is the firstfruits of Achaia to HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"Greet Andronicus and Junia, my countrymen and my fellow prisoners, who are of note among the apostles, who also were in HaMashiach before me."},{"n":9,"text":"Greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in HaMashiach, and Stachys, my beloved."},{"n":10,"text":"Greet Apelles, approved in HaMashiach. Greet those who are of the household of Aristobulus."},{"n":16,"text":"Greet one another with a holy kiss. The churches of HaMashiach greet you."},{"n":18,"text":"For those who are such do not serve our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, but their own belly, and by smooth words and flattering speech deceive the hearts of the simple."},{"n":20,"text":"And the God of peace will crush Satan under your feet shortly. The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you. Amen."},{"n":24,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen."},{"n":25,"text":"Now to Him who is able to establish you according to my gospel and the preaching of YahuShua HaMashiach, according to the revelation of the mystery kept secret since the world began"},{"n":27,"text":"to God, alone wise, be glory through YahuShua HaMashiach forever. Amen."}]},
"1corinthians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, called to be an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach through the will of God, and Sosthenes our brother,"},{"n":2,"text":"To the church of God which is at Corinth, to those who are sanctified in YahuShua HaMashiach, called to be saints, with all who in every place call on the name of YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, both theirs and ours:"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":4,"text":"I thank my God always concerning you for the grace of God which was given to you by YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"even as the testimony of HaMashiach was confirmed in you,"},{"n":7,"text":"so that you come short in no gift, eagerly waiting for the revelation of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":8,"text":"who will also confirm you to the end, that you may be blameless in the day of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":9,"text":"God is faithful, by whom you were called into the fellowship of His Son, YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":10,"text":"Now I plead with you, brethren, by the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that you all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you, but that you be perfectly joined together in the same mind and in the same judgment."},{"n":12,"text":"Now I say this, that each of you says, “I am of Paul,” or “I am of Apollos,” or “I am of Cephas,” or “I am of HaMashiach.”"},{"n":13,"text":"Is HaMashiach divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Or were you baptized in the name of Paul?"},{"n":17,"text":"For HaMashiach did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel, not with wisdom of words, lest the cross of HaMashiach should be made of no effect."},{"n":23,"text":"but we preach HaMashiach crucified, to the Jews a stumbling block and to the Greeks foolishness,"},{"n":24,"text":"but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, HaMashiach the power of God and the wisdom of God."},{"n":30,"text":"But of Him you are in YahuShua HaMashiach, who became for us wisdom from God—and righteousness and sanctification and redemption—"}],"2":[{"n":2,"text":"For I determined not to know anything among you except YahuShua HaMashiach and Him crucified."},{"n":16,"text":"For “who has known the mind of the LORD that he may instruct Him?” But we have the mind of HaMashiach."}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"And I, brethren, could not speak to you as to spiritual people but as to carnal, as to babes in HaMashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"For no other foundation can anyone lay than that which is laid, which is YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":23,"text":"And you are HaMashiach’s, and HaMashiach is God’s."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Let a man so consider us, as servants of HaMashiach and stewards of the mysteries of God."},{"n":10,"text":"We are fools for HaMashiach’s sake, but you are wise in HaMashiach! We are weak, but you are strong! You are distinguished, but we are dishonored!"},{"n":15,"text":"For though you might have ten thousand instructors in HaMashiach, yet you do not have many fathers; for in YahuShua HaMashiach I have begotten you through the gospel."},{"n":17,"text":"For this reason I have sent Timothy to you, who is my beloved and faithful son in the Lord, who will remind you of my ways in HaMashiach, as I teach everywhere in every church."}],"5":[{"n":4,"text":"In the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, when you are gathered together, along with my spirit, with the power of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":5,"text":"deliver such a one to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, that his spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":7,"text":"Therefore purge out the old leaven, that you may be a new lump, since you truly are unleavened. For indeed HaMashiach, our Passover, was sacrificed for us."}],"6":[{"n":11,"text":"And such were some of you. But you were washed, but you were sanctified, but you were justified in the name of the Lord YahuShua and by the Spirit of our God."},{"n":15,"text":"Do you not know that your bodies are members of HaMashiach? Shall I then take the members of HaMashiach and make them members of a harlot? Certainly not!"}],"7":[{"n":22,"text":"For he who is called in the Lord while a slave is the Lord’s freedman. Likewise he who is called while free is HaMashiach’s slave."}],"8":[{"n":6,"text":"yet for us there is one God, the Father, of whom are all things, and we for Him; and one Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, through whom are all things, and through whom we live."},{"n":11,"text":"And because of your knowledge shall the weak brother perish, for whom HaMashiach died?"},{"n":12,"text":"But when you thus sin against the brethren, and wound their weak conscience, you sin against HaMashiach."}],"9":[{"n":1,"text":"Am I not an apostle? Am I not free? Have I not seen YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord? Are you not my work in the Lord?"},{"n":12,"text":"If others are partakers of this right over you, are we not even more? Nevertheless we have not used this right, but endure all things lest we hinder the gospel of HaMashiach."},{"n":18,"text":"What is my reward then? That when I preach the gospel, I may present the gospel of HaMashiach without charge, that I may not abuse my authority in the gospel."},{"n":21,"text":"to those who are without law, as without law (not being without law toward God, but under law toward HaMashiach), that I might win those who are without law;"}],"10":[{"n":4,"text":"and all drank the same spiritual drink. For they drank of that spiritual Rock that followed them, and that Rock was HaMashiach."},{"n":9,"text":"nor let us tempt HaMashiach, as some of them also tempted, and were destroyed by serpents;"},{"n":16,"text":"The cup of blessing which we bless, is it not the communion of the blood of HaMashiach? The bread which we break, is it not the communion of the body of HaMashiach?"}],"11":[{"n":1,"text":"Imitate me, just as I also imitate HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"But I want you to know that the head of every man is HaMashiach, the head of woman is man, and the head of HaMashiach is God."},{"n":23,"text":"For I received from the Lord that which I also delivered to you: that the Lord YahuShua on the same night in which He was betrayed took bread;"}],"12":[{"n":3,"text":"Therefore I make known to you that no one speaking by the Spirit of God calls YahuShua accursed, and no one can say that YahuShua is Lord except by the Holy Spirit."},{"n":12,"text":"For as the body is one and has many members, but all the members of that one body, being many, are one body, so also is HaMashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"Now you are the body of HaMashiach, and members individually."}],"15":[{"n":3,"text":"For I delivered to you first of all that which I also received: that HaMashiach died for our sins according to the Scriptures,"},{"n":12,"text":"Now if HaMashiach is preached that He has been raised from the dead, how do some among you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?"},{"n":13,"text":"But if there is no resurrection of the dead, then HaMashiach is not risen."},{"n":14,"text":"And if HaMashiach is not risen, then our preaching is empty and your faith is also empty."},{"n":15,"text":"Yes, and we are found false witnesses of God, because we have testified of God that He raised up HaMashiach, whom He did not raise up—if in fact the dead do not rise."},{"n":16,"text":"For if the dead do not rise, then HaMashiach is not risen."},{"n":17,"text":"And if HaMashiach is not risen, your faith is futile; you are still in your sins!"},{"n":18,"text":"Then also those who have fallen asleep in HaMashiach have perished."},{"n":19,"text":"If in this life only we have hope in HaMashiach, we are of all men the most pitiable."},{"n":20,"text":"But now HaMashiach is risen from the dead, and has become the firstfruits of those who have fallen asleep."},{"n":22,"text":"For as in Adam all die, even so in HaMashiach all shall be made alive."},{"n":23,"text":"But each one in his own order: HaMashiach the firstfruits, afterward those who are HaMashiach’s at His coming."},{"n":31,"text":"I affirm, by the boasting in you which I have in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord, I die daily."},{"n":57,"text":"But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"16":[{"n":22,"text":"If anyone does not love the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, let him be accursed. O Lord, come!"},{"n":23,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you."},{"n":24,"text":"My love be with you all in YahuShua HaMashiach. Amen."}]},
"2corinthians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, and Timothy our brother, To the church of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints who are in all Achaia:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Father of mercies and God of all comfort,"},{"n":5,"text":"For as the sufferings of HaMashiach abound in us, so our consolation also abounds through HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"(as also you have understood us in part), that we are your boast as you also are ours, in the day of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":19,"text":"For the Son of God, YahuShua HaMashiach, who was preached among you by us—by me, Silvanus, and Timothy—was not Yes and No, but in Him was Yes."},{"n":21,"text":"Now He who establishes us with you in HaMashiach and has anointed us is God,"}],"2":[{"n":10,"text":"Now whom you forgive anything, I also forgive. For if indeed I have forgiven anything, I have forgiven that one for your sakes in the presence of HaMashiach,"},{"n":12,"text":"Furthermore, when I came to Troas to preach HaMashiach’s gospel, and a door was opened to me by the Lord,"},{"n":14,"text":"Now thanks be to God who always leads us in triumph in HaMashiach, and through us diffuses the fragrance of His knowledge in every place."},{"n":15,"text":"For we are to God the fragrance of HaMashiach among those who are being saved and among those who are perishing."},{"n":17,"text":"For we are not, as so many, peddling the word of God; but as of sincerity, but as from God, we speak in the sight of God in HaMashiach."}],"3":[{"n":3,"text":"clearly you are an epistle of HaMashiach, ministered by us, written not with ink but by the Spirit of the living God, not on tablets of stone but on tablets of flesh, that is, of the heart."},{"n":4,"text":"And we have such trust through HaMashiach toward God."},{"n":14,"text":"But their minds were blinded. For until this day the same veil remains unlifted in the reading of the Old Testament, because the veil is taken away in HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":4,"text":"whose minds the god of this age has blinded, who do not believe, lest the light of the gospel of the glory of HaMashiach, who is the image of God, should shine on them."},{"n":5,"text":"For we do not preach ourselves, but YahuShua HaMashiach the Lord, and ourselves your bondservants for YahuShua’s sake."},{"n":6,"text":"For it is the God who commanded light to shine out of darkness, who has shone in our hearts to give the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"always carrying about in the body the dying of the Lord YahuShua, that the life of YahuShua also may be manifested in our body."},{"n":11,"text":"For we who live are always delivered to death for YahuShua’s sake, that the life of YahuShua also may be manifested in our mortal flesh."},{"n":14,"text":"knowing that He who raised up the Lord YahuShua will also raise us up with YahuShua, and will present us with you."}],"5":[{"n":10,"text":"For we must all appear before the judgment seat of HaMashiach, that each one may receive the things done in the body, according to what he has done, whether good or bad."},{"n":14,"text":"For the love of HaMashiach compels us, because we judge thus: that if One died for all, then all died;"},{"n":16,"text":"Therefore, from now on, we regard no one according to the flesh. Even though we have known HaMashiach according to the flesh, yet now we know Him thus no longer."},{"n":17,"text":"Therefore, if anyone is in HaMashiach, he is a new creation; old things have passed away; behold, all things have become new."},{"n":18,"text":"Now all things are of God, who has reconciled us to Himself through YahuShua HaMashiach, and has given us the ministry of reconciliation,"},{"n":19,"text":"that is, that God was in HaMashiach reconciling the world to Himself, not imputing their trespasses to them, and has committed to us the word of reconciliation."},{"n":20,"text":"Now then, we are ambassadors for HaMashiach, as though God were pleading through us: we implore you on HaMashiach’s behalf, be reconciled to God."}],"6":[{"n":15,"text":"And what accord has HaMashiach with Belial? Or what part has a believer with an unbeliever?"}],"8":[{"n":9,"text":"For you know the grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that though He was rich, yet for your sakes He became poor, that you through His poverty might become rich."},{"n":23,"text":"If anyone inquires about Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker concerning you. Or if our brethren are inquired about, they are messengers of the churches, the glory of HaMashiach."}],"9":[{"n":13,"text":"while, through the proof of this ministry, they glorify God for the obedience of your confession to the gospel of HaMashiach, and for your liberal sharing with them and all men,"}],"10":[{"n":1,"text":"Now I, Paul, myself am pleading with you by the meekness and gentleness of HaMashiach— who in presence am lowly among you, but being absent am bold toward you."},{"n":5,"text":"casting down arguments and every high thing that exalts itself against the knowledge of God, bringing every thought into captivity to the obedience of HaMashiach,"},{"n":7,"text":"Do you look at things according to the outward appearance? If anyone is convinced in himself that he is HaMashiach’s, let him again consider this in himself, that just as he is HaMashiach’s, even so we are HaMashiach’s."},{"n":14,"text":"For we are not overextending ourselves (as though our authority did not extend to you), for it was to you that we came with the gospel of HaMashiach;"}],"11":[{"n":2,"text":"For I am jealous for you with godly jealousy. For I have betrothed you to one husband, that I may present you as a chaste virgin to HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"But I fear, lest somehow, as the serpent deceived Eve by his craftiness, so your minds may be corrupted from the simplicity that is in HaMashiach."},{"n":4,"text":"For if he who comes preaches another YahuShua whom we have not preached, or if you receive a different spirit which you have not received, or a different gospel which you have not accepted—you may well put up with it!"},{"n":10,"text":"As the truth of HaMashiach is in me, no one shall stop me from this boasting in the regions of Achaia."},{"n":13,"text":"For such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into apostles of HaMashiach."},{"n":23,"text":"Are they ministers of HaMashiach?—I speak as a fool—I am more: in labors more abundant, in stripes above measure, in prisons more frequently, in deaths often."},{"n":31,"text":"The God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who is blessed forever, knows that I am not lying."}],"12":[{"n":2,"text":"I know a man in HaMashiach who fourteen years ago—whether in the body I do not know, or whether out of the body I do not know, God knows—such a one was caught up to the third heaven."},{"n":9,"text":"And He said to me, “My grace is sufficient for you, for My strength is made perfect in weakness.” Therefore most gladly I will rather boast in my infirmities, that the power of HaMashiach may rest upon me."},{"n":10,"text":"Therefore I take pleasure in infirmities, in reproaches, in needs, in persecutions, in distresses, for HaMashiach’s sake. For when I am weak, then I am strong."},{"n":19,"text":"Again, do you think that we excuse ourselves to you? We speak before God in HaMashiach. But we do all things, beloved, for your edification."}],"13":[{"n":3,"text":"since you seek a proof of HaMashiach speaking in me, who is not weak toward you, but mighty in you."},{"n":5,"text":"Examine yourselves as to whether you are in the faith. Test yourselves. Do you not know yourselves, that YahuShua HaMashiach is in you?—unless indeed you are disqualified."},{"n":14,"text":"The grace of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and the love of God, and the communion of the Holy Spirit be with you all. Amen."}]},
"galatians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle (not from men nor through man, but through YahuShua HaMashiach and God the Father who raised Him from the dead),"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God the Father and our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"I marvel that you are turning away so soon from Him who called you in the grace of HaMashiach, to a different gospel,"},{"n":7,"text":"which is not another; but there are some who trouble you and want to pervert the gospel of HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"For do I now persuade men, or God? Or do I seek to please men? For if I still pleased men, I would not be a bondservant of HaMashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"For I neither received it from man, nor was I taught it, but it came through the revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":22,"text":"And I was unknown by face to the churches of Judea which were in HaMashiach."}],"2":[{"n":4,"text":"And this occurred because of false brethren secretly brought in (who came in by stealth to spy out our liberty which we have in YahuShua HaMashiach, that they might bring us into bondage),"},{"n":16,"text":"knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law but by faith in YahuShua HaMashiach, even we have believed in YahuShua HaMashiach, that we might be justified by faith in HaMashiach and not by the works of the law; for by the works of the law no flesh shall be justified."},{"n":17,"text":"“But if, while we seek to be justified by HaMashiach, we ourselves also are found sinners, is HaMashiach therefore a minister of sin? Certainly not!"},{"n":20,"text":"I have been crucified with HaMashiach; it is no longer I who live, but HaMashiach lives in me; and the life which I now live in the flesh I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave Himself for me."},{"n":21,"text":"I do not set aside the grace of God; for if righteousness comes through the law, then HaMashiach died in vain.”"}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"O foolish Galatians! Who has bewitched you that you should not obey the truth, before whose eyes YahuShua HaMashiach was clearly portrayed among you as crucified?"},{"n":13,"text":"HaMashiach has redeemed us from the curse of the law, having become a curse for us (for it is written, “Cursed is everyone who hangs on a tree”),"},{"n":14,"text":"that the blessing of Abraham might come upon the Gentiles in YahuShua HaMashiach, that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith."},{"n":16,"text":"Now to Abraham and his Seed were the promises made. He does not say, “And to seeds,” as of many, but as of one, “And to your Seed,” who is HaMashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"And this I say, that the law, which was four hundred and thirty years later, cannot annul the covenant that was confirmed before by God in HaMashiach, that it should make the promise of no effect."},{"n":22,"text":"But the Scripture has confined all under sin, that the promise by faith in YahuShua HaMashiach might be given to those who believe."},{"n":24,"text":"Therefore the law was our tutor to bring us to HaMashiach, that we might be justified by faith."},{"n":26,"text":"For you are all sons of God through faith in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":27,"text":"For as many of you as were baptized into HaMashiach have put on HaMashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither slave nor free, there is neither male nor female; for you are all one in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":29,"text":"And if you are HaMashiach’s, then you are Abraham’s seed, and heirs according to the promise."}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"Therefore you are no longer a slave but a son, and if a son, then an heir of God through HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"And my trial which was in my flesh you did not despise or reject, but you received me as an angel of God, even as YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":19,"text":"My little children, for whom I labor in birth again until HaMashiach is formed in you,"}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Stand fast therefore in the liberty by which HaMashiach has made us free, and do not be entangled again with a yoke of bondage."},{"n":2,"text":"Indeed I, Paul, say to you that if you become circumcised, HaMashiach will profit you nothing."},{"n":4,"text":"You have become estranged from HaMashiach, you who attempt to be justified by law; you have fallen from grace."},{"n":6,"text":"For in YahuShua HaMashiach neither circumcision nor uncircumcision avails anything, but faith working through love."},{"n":24,"text":"And those who are HaMashiach’s have crucified the flesh with its passions and desires."}],"6":[{"n":2,"text":"Bear one another’s burdens, and so fulfill the law of HaMashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"As many as desire to make a good showing in the flesh, these would compel you to be circumcised, only that they may not suffer persecution for the cross of HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"But God forbid that I should boast except in the cross of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, by whom the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world."},{"n":15,"text":"For in YahuShua HaMashiach neither circumcision nor uncircumcision avails anything, but a new creation."},{"n":17,"text":"From now on let no one trouble me, for I bear in my body the marks of the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":18,"text":"Brethren, the grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with your spirit. Amen."}]},
"ephesians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, To the saints who are in Ephesus, and faithful in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places in HaMashiach,"},{"n":5,"text":"having predestined us to adoption as sons by YahuShua HaMashiach to Himself, according to the good pleasure of His will,"},{"n":10,"text":"that in the dispensation of the fullness of the times He might gather together in one all things in HaMashiach, both which are in heaven and which are on earth—in Him."},{"n":12,"text":"that we who first trusted in HaMashiach should be to the praise of His glory."},{"n":15,"text":"Therefore I also, after I heard of your faith in the Lord YahuShua and your love for all the saints,"},{"n":17,"text":"that the God of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Father of glory, may give to you the spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of Him,"},{"n":20,"text":"which He worked in HaMashiach when He raised Him from the dead and seated Him at His right hand in the heavenly places,"}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"even when we were dead in trespasses, made us alive together with HaMashiach (by grace you have been saved),"},{"n":6,"text":"and raised us up together, and made us sit together in the heavenly places in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":7,"text":"that in the ages to come He might show the exceeding riches of His grace in His kindness toward us in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"For we are His workmanship, created in YahuShua HaMashiach for good works, which God prepared beforehand that we should walk in them."},{"n":12,"text":"that at that time you were without HaMashiach, being aliens from the commonwealth of Israel and strangers from the covenants of promise, having no hope and without God in the world."},{"n":13,"text":"But now in YahuShua HaMashiach you who once were far off have been brought near by the blood of HaMashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"having been built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, YahuShua HaMashiach Himself being the chief cornerstone,"}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach for you Gentiles—"},{"n":4,"text":"by which, when you read, you may understand my knowledge in the mystery of HaMashiach),"},{"n":6,"text":"that the Gentiles should be fellow heirs, of the same body, and partakers of His promise in HaMashiach through the gospel,"},{"n":8,"text":"To me, who am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given, that I should preach among the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of HaMashiach,"},{"n":9,"text":"and to make all see what is the fellowship of the mystery, which from the beginning of the ages has been hidden in God who created all things through YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":11,"text":"according to the eternal purpose which He accomplished in YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord,"},{"n":14,"text":"For this reason I bow my knees to the Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":17,"text":"that HaMashiach may dwell in your hearts through faith; that you, being rooted and grounded in love,"},{"n":19,"text":"to know the love of HaMashiach which passes knowledge; that you may be filled with all the fullness of God."},{"n":21,"text":"to Him be glory in the church by YahuShua HaMashiach to all generations, forever and ever. Amen."}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"But to each one of us grace was given according to the measure of HaMashiach’s gift."},{"n":12,"text":"for the equipping of the saints for the work of ministry, for the edifying of the body of HaMashiach,"},{"n":13,"text":"till we all come to the unity of the faith and of the knowledge of the Son of God, to a perfect man, to the measure of the stature of the fullness of HaMashiach;"},{"n":15,"text":"but, speaking the truth in love, may grow up in all things into Him who is the head—HaMashiach—"},{"n":20,"text":"But you have not so learned HaMashiach,"},{"n":21,"text":"if indeed you have heard Him and have been taught by Him, as the truth is in YahuShua:"},{"n":32,"text":"And be kind to one another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God in HaMashiach forgave you."}],"5":[{"n":2,"text":"And walk in love, as HaMashiach also has loved us and given Himself for us, an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweet-smelling aroma."},{"n":5,"text":"For this you know, that no fornicator, unclean person, nor covetous man, who is an idolater, has any inheritance in the kingdom of HaMashiach and God."},{"n":14,"text":"Therefore He says: “Awake, you who sleep, Arise from the dead, And HaMashiach will give you light.”"},{"n":20,"text":"giving thanks always for all things to God the Father in the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":23,"text":"For the husband is head of the wife, as also HaMashiach is head of the church; and He is the Savior of the body."},{"n":24,"text":"Therefore, just as the church is subject to HaMashiach, so let the wives be to their own husbands in everything."},{"n":25,"text":"Husbands, love your wives, just as HaMashiach also loved the church and gave Himself for her,"},{"n":32,"text":"This is a great mystery, but I speak concerning HaMashiach and the church."}],"6":[{"n":5,"text":"Bondservants, be obedient to those who are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in sincerity of heart, as to HaMashiach;"},{"n":6,"text":"not with eyeservice, as men-pleasers, but as bondservants of HaMashiach, doing the will of God from the heart,"},{"n":23,"text":"Peace to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":24,"text":"Grace be with all those who love our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach in sincerity. Amen."}]},
"philippians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul and Timothy, bondservants of YahuShua HaMashiach, To all the saints in YahuShua HaMashiach who are in Philippi, with the bishops and deacons:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"being confident of this very thing, that He who has begun a good work in you will complete it until the day of YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":8,"text":"For God is my witness, how greatly I long for you all with the affection of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":10,"text":"that you may approve the things that are excellent, that you may be sincere and without offense till the day of HaMashiach,"},{"n":11,"text":"being filled with the fruits of righteousness which are by YahuShua HaMashiach, to the glory and praise of God."},{"n":13,"text":"so that it has become evident to the whole palace guard, and to all the rest, that my chains are in HaMashiach;"},{"n":15,"text":"Some indeed preach HaMashiach even from envy and strife, and some also from goodwill:"},{"n":16,"text":"The former preach HaMashiach from selfish ambition, not sincerely, supposing to add affliction to my chains;"},{"n":18,"text":"What then? Only that in every way, whether in pretense or in truth, HaMashiach is preached; and in this I rejoice, yes, and will rejoice."},{"n":19,"text":"For I know that this will turn out for my deliverance through your prayer and the supply of the Spirit of YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":20,"text":"according to my earnest expectation and hope that in nothing I shall be ashamed, but with all boldness, as always, so now also HaMashiach will be magnified in my body, whether by life or by death."},{"n":21,"text":"For to me, to live is HaMashiach, and to die is gain."},{"n":23,"text":"For I am hard-pressed between the two, having a desire to depart and be with HaMashiach, which is far better."},{"n":26,"text":"that your rejoicing for me may be more abundant in YahuShua HaMashiach by my coming to you again."},{"n":27,"text":"Only let your conduct be worthy of the gospel of HaMashiach, so that whether I come and see you or am absent, I may hear of your affairs, that you stand fast in one spirit, with one mind striving together for the faith of the gospel,"},{"n":29,"text":"For to you it has been granted on behalf of HaMashiach, not only to believe in Him, but also to suffer for His sake,"}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore if there is any consolation in HaMashiach, if any comfort of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any affection and mercy,"},{"n":5,"text":"Let this mind be in you which was also in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":10,"text":"that at the name of YahuShua every knee should bow, of those in heaven, and of those on earth, and of those under the earth,"},{"n":11,"text":"and that every tongue should confess that YahuShua HaMashiach is Lord, to the glory of God the Father."},{"n":16,"text":"holding fast the word of life, so that I may rejoice in the day of HaMashiach that I have not run in vain or labored in vain."},{"n":19,"text":"But I trust in the Lord YahuShua to send Timothy to you shortly, that I also may be encouraged when I know your state."},{"n":21,"text":"For all seek their own, not the things which are of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":30,"text":"because for the work of HaMashiach he came close to death, not regarding his life, to supply what was lacking in your service toward me."}],"3":[{"n":3,"text":"For we are the circumcision, who worship God in the Spirit, rejoice in YahuShua HaMashiach, and have no confidence in the flesh,"},{"n":7,"text":"But what things were gain to me, these I have counted loss for HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Yet indeed I also count all things loss for the excellence of the knowledge of YahuShua HaMashiach my Lord, for whom I have suffered the loss of all things, and count them as rubbish, that I may gain HaMashiach"},{"n":9,"text":"and be found in Him, not having my own righteousness, which is from the law, but that which is through faith in HaMashiach, the righteousness which is from God by faith;"},{"n":12,"text":"Not that I have already attained, or am already perfected; but I press on, that I may lay hold of that for which YahuShua HaMashiach has also laid hold of me."},{"n":14,"text":"I press toward the goal for the prize of the upward call of God in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":18,"text":"For many walk, of whom I have told you often, and now tell you even weeping, that they are the enemies of the cross of HaMashiach:"},{"n":20,"text":"For our citizenship is in heaven, from which we also eagerly wait for the Savior, the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"}],"4":[{"n":7,"text":"and the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and minds through YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":13,"text":"I can do all things through HaMashiach who strengthens me."},{"n":19,"text":"And my God shall supply all your need according to His riches in glory by YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"Greet every saint in YahuShua HaMashiach. The brethren who are with me greet you."},{"n":23,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen."}]},
"colossians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, and Timothy our brother,"},{"n":2,"text":"To the saints and faithful brethren in HaMashiach who are in Colosse: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"We give thanks to the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, praying always for you,"},{"n":4,"text":"since we heard of your faith in YahuShua HaMashiach and of your love for all the saints;"},{"n":7,"text":"as you also learned from Epaphras, our dear fellow servant, who is a faithful minister of HaMashiach on your behalf,"},{"n":24,"text":"I now rejoice in my sufferings for you, and fill up in my flesh what is lacking in the afflictions of HaMashiach, for the sake of His body, which is the church,"},{"n":27,"text":"To them God willed to make known what are the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles: which is HaMashiach in you, the hope of glory."},{"n":28,"text":"Him we preach, warning every man and teaching every man in all wisdom, that we may present every man perfect in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"2":[{"n":2,"text":"that their hearts may be encouraged, being knit together in love, and attaining to all riches of the full assurance of understanding, to the knowledge of the mystery of God, both of the Father and of HaMashiach,"},{"n":5,"text":"For though I am absent in the flesh, yet I am with you in spirit, rejoicing to see your good order and the steadfastness of your faith in HaMashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"As you therefore have received YahuShua HaMashiach the Lord, so walk in Him,"},{"n":8,"text":"Beware lest anyone cheat you through philosophy and empty deceit, according to the tradition of men, according to the basic principles of the world, and not according to HaMashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"In Him you were also circumcised with the circumcision made without hands, by putting off the body of the sins of the flesh, by the circumcision of HaMashiach,"},{"n":17,"text":"which are a shadow of things to come, but the substance is of HaMashiach."},{"n":20,"text":"Therefore, if you died with HaMashiach from the basic principles of the world, why, as though living in the world, do you subject yourselves to regulations—"}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"If then you were raised with HaMashiach, seek those things which are above, where HaMashiach is, sitting at the right hand of God."},{"n":3,"text":"For you died, and your life is hidden with HaMashiach in God."},{"n":4,"text":"When HaMashiach who is our life appears, then you also will appear with Him in glory."},{"n":11,"text":"where there is neither Greek nor Jew, circumcised nor uncircumcised, barbarian, Scythian, slave nor free, but HaMashiach is all and in all."},{"n":13,"text":"bearing with one another, and forgiving one another, if anyone has a complaint against another; even as HaMashiach forgave you, so you also must do."},{"n":16,"text":"Let the word of HaMashiach dwell in you richly in all wisdom, teaching and admonishing one another in psalms and hymns and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your hearts to the Lord."},{"n":17,"text":"And whatever you do in word or deed, do all in the name of the Lord YahuShua, giving thanks to God the Father through Him."},{"n":24,"text":"knowing that from the Lord you will receive the reward of the inheritance; for you serve the Lord HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":3,"text":"meanwhile praying also for us, that God would open to us a door for the word, to speak the mystery of HaMashiach, for which I am also in chains,"},{"n":12,"text":"Epaphras, who is one of you, a bondservant of HaMashiach, greets you, always laboring fervently for you in prayers, that you may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God."}]},
"1thessalonians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"remembering without ceasing your work of faith, labor of love, and patience of hope in our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach in the sight of our God and Father,"},{"n":10,"text":"and to wait for His Son from heaven, whom He raised from the dead, even YahuShua who delivers us from the wrath to come."}],"2":[{"n":6,"text":"Nor did we seek glory from men, either from you or from others, when we might have made demands as apostles of HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"For you, brethren, became imitators of the churches of God which are in Judea in YahuShua HaMashiach. For you also suffered the same things from your own countrymen, just as they did from the Judeans,"},{"n":15,"text":"who killed both the Lord YahuShua and their own prophets, and have persecuted us; and they do not please God and are contrary to all men,"},{"n":19,"text":"For what is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing? Is it not even you in the presence of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach at His coming?"}],"3":[{"n":2,"text":"and sent Timothy, our brother and minister of God, and our fellow laborer in the gospel of HaMashiach, to establish you and encourage you concerning your faith,"},{"n":11,"text":"Now may our God and Father Himself, and our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, direct our way to you."},{"n":13,"text":"so that He may establish your hearts blameless in holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach with all His saints."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Finally then, brethren, we urge and exhort in the Lord YahuShua that you should abound more and more, just as you received from us how you ought to walk and to please God;"},{"n":2,"text":"for you know what commandments we gave you through the Lord YahuShua."},{"n":14,"text":"For if we believe that YahuShua died and rose again, even so God will bring with Him those who sleep in YahuShua."},{"n":16,"text":"For the Lord Himself will descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of an archangel, and with the trumpet of God. And the dead in HaMashiach will rise first."}],"5":[{"n":9,"text":"For God did not appoint us to wrath, but to obtain salvation through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":18,"text":"in everything give thanks; for this is the will of God in YahuShua HaMashiach for you."},{"n":23,"text":"Now may the God of peace Himself sanctify you completely; and may your whole spirit, soul, and body be preserved blameless at the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":28,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you. Amen."}]},
"2thessalonians":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, To the church of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"and to give you who are troubled rest with us when the Lord YahuShua is revealed from heaven with His mighty angels,"},{"n":8,"text":"in flaming fire taking vengeance on those who do not know God, and on those who do not obey the gospel of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":12,"text":"that the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach may be glorified in you, and you in Him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"Now, brethren, concerning the coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach and our gathering together to Him, we ask you,"},{"n":2,"text":"not to be soon shaken in mind or troubled, either by spirit or by word or by letter, as if from us, as though the day of HaMashiach had come."},{"n":14,"text":"to which He called you by our gospel, for the obtaining of the glory of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":16,"text":"Now may our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach Himself, and our God and Father, who has loved us and given us everlasting consolation and good hope by grace,"}],"3":[{"n":5,"text":"Now may the Lord direct your hearts into the love of God and into the patience of HaMashiach."},{"n":6,"text":"But we command you, brethren, in the name of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, that you withdraw from every brother who walks disorderly and not according to the tradition which he received from us."},{"n":12,"text":"Now those who are such we command and exhort through our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach that they work in quietness and eat their own bread."},{"n":18,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen."}]},
"1timothy":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, by the commandment of God our Savior and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, our hope,"},{"n":2,"text":"To Timothy, a true son in the faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God our Father and YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":12,"text":"And I thank YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord who has enabled me, because He counted me faithful, putting me into the ministry,"},{"n":14,"text":"And the grace of our Lord was exceedingly abundant, with faith and love which are in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":15,"text":"This is a faithful saying and worthy of all acceptance, that YahuShua HaMashiach came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am chief."},{"n":16,"text":"However, for this reason I obtained mercy, that in me first YahuShua HaMashiach might show all longsuffering, as a pattern to those who are going to believe on Him for everlasting life."}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"For there is one God and one Mediator between God and men, the Man YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":7,"text":"for which I was appointed a preacher and an apostle—I am speaking the truth in HaMashiach and not lying— a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and truth."}],"3":[{"n":13,"text":"For those who have served well as deacons obtain for themselves a good standing and great boldness in the faith which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":6,"text":"If you instruct the brethren in these things, you will be a good minister of YahuShua HaMashiach, nourished in the words of faith and of the good doctrine which you have carefully followed."}],"5":[{"n":11,"text":"But refuse the younger widows; for when they have begun to grow wanton against HaMashiach, they desire to marry,"},{"n":21,"text":"I charge you before God and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach and the elect angels that you observe these things without prejudice, doing nothing with partiality."}],"6":[{"n":3,"text":"If anyone teaches otherwise and does not consent to wholesome words, even the words of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, and to the doctrine which accords with godliness,"},{"n":13,"text":"I urge you in the sight of God who gives life to all things, and before YahuShua HaMashiach who witnessed the good confession before Pontius Pilate,"},{"n":14,"text":"that you keep this commandment without spot, blameless until our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach’s appearing,"}]},
"2timothy":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach by the will of God, according to the promise of life which is in YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":2,"text":"To Timothy, a beloved son: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and YahuShua HaMashiach our Lord."},{"n":9,"text":"who has saved us and called us with a holy calling, not according to our works, but according to His own purpose and grace which was given to us in YahuShua HaMashiach before time began,"},{"n":10,"text":"but has now been revealed by the appearing of our Savior YahuShua HaMashiach, who has abolished death and brought life and immortality to light through the gospel,"},{"n":13,"text":"Hold fast the pattern of sound words which you have heard from me, in faith and love which are in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"You therefore, my son, be strong in the grace that is in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":3,"text":"You therefore must endure hardship as a good soldier of YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Remember that YahuShua HaMashiach, of the seed of David, was raised from the dead according to my gospel,"},{"n":10,"text":"Therefore I endure all things for the sake of the elect, that they also may obtain the salvation which is in YahuShua HaMashiach with eternal glory."},{"n":19,"text":"Nevertheless the solid foundation of God stands, having this seal: “The Lord knows those who are His,” and, “Let everyone who names the name of HaMashiach depart from iniquity.”"}],"3":[{"n":12,"text":"Yes, and all who desire to live godly in YahuShua HaMashiach will suffer persecution."},{"n":15,"text":"and that from childhood you have known the Holy Scriptures, which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith which is in YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"I charge you therefore before God and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who will judge the living and the dead at His appearing and His kingdom:"},{"n":22,"text":"The Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with your spirit. Grace be with you. Amen."}]},
"titus":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a bondservant of God and an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, according to the faith of God’s elect and the acknowledgment of the truth which accords with godliness,"},{"n":4,"text":"To Titus, a true son in our common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach our Savior."}],"2":[{"n":13,"text":"looking for the blessed hope and glorious appearing of our great God and Savior YahuShua HaMashiach,"}],"3":[{"n":6,"text":"whom He poured out on us abundantly through YahuShua HaMashiach our Savior,"}]},
"philemon":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Paul, a prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach, and Timothy our brother, To Philemon our beloved friend and fellow laborer,"},{"n":3,"text":"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":5,"text":"hearing of your love and faith which you have toward the Lord YahuShua and toward all the saints,"},{"n":6,"text":"that the sharing of your faith may become effective by the acknowledgment of every good thing which is in you in YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":8,"text":"Therefore, though I might be very bold in HaMashiach to command you what is fitting,"},{"n":9,"text":"yet for love’s sake I rather appeal to you—being such a one as Paul, the aged, and now also a prisoner of YahuShua HaMashiach—"},{"n":23,"text":"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in YahuShua HaMashiach, greets you,"},{"n":25,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with your spirit. Amen."}]},
"hebrews":{"2":[{"n":9,"text":"But we see YahuShua, who was made a little lower than the angels, for the suffering of death crowned with glory and honor, that He, by the grace of God, might taste death for everyone."}],"3":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore, holy brethren, partakers of the heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our confession, YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":6,"text":"but HaMashiach as a Son over His own house, whose house we are if we hold fast the confidence and the rejoicing of the hope firm to the end."},{"n":14,"text":"For we have become partakers of HaMashiach if we hold the beginning of our confidence steadfast to the end,"}],"4":[{"n":14,"text":"Seeing then that we have a great High Priest who has passed through the heavens, YahuShua the Son of God, let us hold fast our confession."}],"5":[{"n":5,"text":"So also HaMashiach did not glorify Himself to become High Priest, but it was He who said to Him: “You are My Son, Today I have begotten You.”"}],"6":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore, leaving the discussion of the elementary principles of HaMashiach, let us go on to perfection, not laying again the foundation of repentance from dead works and of faith toward God,"},{"n":20,"text":"where the forerunner has entered for us, even YahuShua, having become High Priest forever according to the order of Melchizedek."}],"7":[{"n":22,"text":"by so much more YahuShua has become a surety of a better covenant."}],"9":[{"n":11,"text":"But HaMashiach came as High Priest of the good things to come, with the greater and more perfect tabernacle not made with hands, that is, not of this creation."},{"n":14,"text":"how much more shall the blood of HaMashiach, who through the eternal Spirit offered Himself without spot to God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?"},{"n":24,"text":"For HaMashiach has not entered the holy places made with hands, which are copies of the true, but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God for us;"},{"n":28,"text":"so HaMashiach was offered once to bear the sins of many. To those who eagerly wait for Him He will appear a second time, apart from sin, for salvation."}],"10":[{"n":10,"text":"By that will we have been sanctified through the offering of the body of YahuShua HaMashiach once for all."},{"n":19,"text":"Therefore, brethren, having boldness to enter the Holiest by the blood of YahuShua,"}],"11":[{"n":26,"text":"esteeming the reproach of HaMashiach greater riches than the treasures in Egypt; for he looked to the reward."}],"12":[{"n":2,"text":"looking unto YahuShua, the author and finisher of our faith, who for the joy that was set before Him endured the cross, despising the shame, and has sat down at the right hand of the throne of God."},{"n":24,"text":"to YahuShua the Mediator of the new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling that speaks better things than that of Abel."}],"13":[{"n":8,"text":"YahuShua HaMashiach is the same yesterday, today, and forever."},{"n":12,"text":"Therefore YahuShua also, that He might sanctify the people with His own blood, suffered outside the gate."},{"n":20,"text":"Now may the God of peace who brought up our Lord YahuShua from the dead, that great Shepherd of the sheep, through the blood of the everlasting covenant,"},{"n":21,"text":"make you complete in every good work to do His will, working in you what is well pleasing in His sight, through YahuShua HaMashiach, to whom be glory forever and ever. Amen."}]},
"james":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"James, a bondservant of God and of the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, To the twelve tribes which are scattered abroad: Greetings."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"My brethren, do not hold the faith of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Lord of glory, with partiality."}]},
"1peter":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Peter, an apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, To the pilgrims of the Dispersion in Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,"},{"n":2,"text":"elect according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, in sanctification of the Spirit, for obedience and sprinkling of the blood of YahuShua HaMashiach: Grace to you and peace be multiplied."},{"n":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, who according to His abundant mercy has begotten us again to a living hope through the resurrection of YahuShua HaMashiach from the dead,"},{"n":7,"text":"that the genuineness of your faith, being much more precious than gold that perishes, though it is tested by fire, may be found to praise, honor, and glory at the revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach,"},{"n":11,"text":"searching what, or what manner of time, the Spirit of HaMashiach who was in them was indicating when He testified beforehand the sufferings of HaMashiach and the glories that would follow."},{"n":13,"text":"Therefore gird up the loins of your mind, be sober, and rest your hope fully upon the grace that is to be brought to you at the revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach;"},{"n":19,"text":"but with the precious blood of HaMashiach, as of a lamb without blemish and without spot."}],"2":[{"n":5,"text":"you also, as living stones, are being built up a spiritual house, a holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices acceptable to God through YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":21,"text":"For to this you were called, because HaMashiach also suffered for us, leaving us an example, that you should follow His steps:"}],"3":[{"n":16,"text":"having a good conscience, that when they defame you as evildoers, those who revile your good conduct in HaMashiach may be ashamed."},{"n":18,"text":"For HaMashiach also suffered once for sins, the just for the unjust, that He might bring us to God, being put to death in the flesh but made alive by the Spirit,"},{"n":21,"text":"There is also an antitype which now saves us—baptism (not the removal of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God), through the resurrection of YahuShua HaMashiach,"}],"4":[{"n":1,"text":"Therefore, since HaMashiach suffered for us in the flesh, arm yourselves also with the same mind, for he who has suffered in the flesh has ceased from sin,"},{"n":11,"text":"If anyone speaks, let him speak as the oracles of God. If anyone ministers, let him do it as with the ability which God supplies, that in all things God may be glorified through YahuShua HaMashiach, to whom belong the glory and the dominion forever and ever. Amen."},{"n":13,"text":"but rejoice to the extent that you partake of HaMashiach’s sufferings, that when His glory is revealed, you may also be glad with exceeding joy."},{"n":14,"text":"If you are reproached for the name of HaMashiach, blessed are you, for the Spirit of glory and of God rests upon you. On their part He is blasphemed, but on your part He is glorified."}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"The elders who are among you I exhort, I who am a fellow elder and a witness of the sufferings of HaMashiach, and also a partaker of the glory that will be revealed:"},{"n":10,"text":"But may the God of all grace, who called us to His eternal glory by YahuShua HaMashiach, after you have suffered a while, perfect, establish, strengthen, and settle you."},{"n":14,"text":"Greet one another with a kiss of love. Peace to you all who are in YahuShua HaMashiach. Amen."}]},
"2peter":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Simon Peter, a bondservant and apostle of YahuShua HaMashiach, To those who have obtained like precious faith with us by the righteousness of our God and Savior YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":2,"text":"Grace and peace be multiplied to you in the knowledge of God and of YahuShua our Lord,"},{"n":8,"text":"For if these things are yours and abound, you will be neither barren nor unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":11,"text":"for so an entrance will be supplied to you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Savior YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":14,"text":"knowing that shortly I must put off my tent, just as our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach showed me."},{"n":16,"text":"For we did not follow cunningly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, but were eyewitnesses of His majesty."}],"2":[{"n":20,"text":"For if, after they have escaped the pollutions of the world through the knowledge of the Lord and Savior YahuShua HaMashiach, they are again entangled in them and overcome, the latter end is worse for them than the beginning."}],"3":[{"n":18,"text":"but grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior YahuShua HaMashiach. To Him be the glory both now and forever. Amen."}]},
"1john":{"1":[{"n":3,"text":"that which we have seen and heard we declare to you, that you also may have fellowship with us; and truly our fellowship is with the Father and with His Son YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":7,"text":"But if we walk in the light as He is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of YahuShua HaMashiach His Son cleanses us from all sin."}],"2":[{"n":1,"text":"My little children, these things I write to you, so that you may not sin. And if anyone sins, we have an Advocate with the Father, YahuShua HaMashiach the righteous."},{"n":22,"text":"Who is a liar but he who denies that YahuShua is HaMashiach? He is antichrist who denies the Father and the Son."}],"3":[{"n":23,"text":"And this is His commandment: that we should believe on the name of His Son YahuShua HaMashiach and love one another, as He gave us commandment."}],"4":[{"n":2,"text":"By this you know the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesses that YahuShua HaMashiach has come in the flesh is of God,"},{"n":3,"text":"and every spirit that does not confess that YahuShua HaMashiach has come in the flesh is not of God. And this is the spirit of the Antichrist, which you have heard was coming, and is now already in the world."},{"n":15,"text":"Whoever confesses that YahuShua is the Son of God, God abides in him, and he in God."}],"5":[{"n":1,"text":"Whoever believes that YahuShua is HaMashiach is born of God, and everyone who loves Him who begot also loves him who is begotten of Him."},{"n":5,"text":"Who is he who overcomes the world, but he who believes that YahuShua is the Son of God?"},{"n":6,"text":"This is He who came by water and blood—YahuShua HaMashiach; not only by water, but by water and blood. And it is the Spirit who bears witness, because the Spirit is truth."},{"n":20,"text":"And we know that the Son of God has come and has given us an understanding, that we may know Him who is true; and we are in Him who is true, in His Son YahuShua HaMashiach. This is the true God and eternal life."}]},
"2john":{"1":[{"n":3,"text":"Grace, mercy, and peace will be with you from God the Father and from the Lord YahuShua HaMashiach, the Son of the Father, in truth and love."},{"n":7,"text":"For many deceivers have gone out into the world who do not confess YahuShua HaMashiach as coming in the flesh. This is a deceiver and an antichrist."},{"n":9,"text":"Whoever transgresses and does not abide in the doctrine of HaMashiach does not have God. He who abides in the doctrine of HaMashiach has both the Father and the Son."}]},
"jude":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"Jude, a bondservant of YahuShua HaMashiach, and brother of James, To those who are called, sanctified by God the Father, and preserved in YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":4,"text":"For certain men have crept in unnoticed, who long ago were marked out for this condemnation, ungodly men, who turn the grace of our God into lewdness and deny the only Lord God and our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach."},{"n":17,"text":"But you, beloved, remember the words which were spoken before by the apostles of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach:"},{"n":21,"text":"keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach unto eternal life."}]},
"revelation":{"1":[{"n":1,"text":"The Revelation of YahuShua HaMashiach, which God gave Him to show His servants—things which must shortly take place. And He sent and signified it by His angel to His servant John,"},{"n":2,"text":"who bore witness to the word of God, and to the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach, to all things that he saw."},{"n":5,"text":"and from YahuShua HaMashiach, the faithful witness, the firstborn from the dead, and the ruler over the kings of the earth. To Him who loved us and washed us from our sins in His own blood,"},{"n":9,"text":"I, John, both your brother and companion in the tribulation and kingdom and patience of YahuShua HaMashiach, was on the island that is called Patmos for the word of God and for the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"11":[{"n":15,"text":"Then the seventh angel sounded: And there were loud voices in heaven, saying, “The kingdoms of this world have become the kingdoms of our Lord and of His Mashiach, and He shall reign forever and ever!”"}],"12":[{"n":10,"text":"Then I heard a loud voice saying in heaven, “Now salvation, and strength, and the kingdom of our God, and the power of His Mashiach have come, for the accuser of our brethren, who accused them before our God day and night, has been cast down."},{"n":17,"text":"And the dragon was enraged with the woman, and he went to make war with the rest of her offspring, who keep the commandments of God and have the testimony of YahuShua HaMashiach."}],"14":[{"n":12,"text":"Here is the patience of the saints; here are those who keep the commandments of God and the faith of YahuShua."}],"17":[{"n":6,"text":"I saw the woman, drunk with the blood of the saints and with the blood of the martyrs of YahuShua. And when I saw her, I marveled with great amazement."}],"19":[{"n":10,"text":"And I fell at his feet to worship him. But he said to me, “See that you do not do that! I am your fellow servant, and of your brethren who have the testimony of YahuShua. Worship God! For the testimony of YahuShua is the spirit of prophecy.”"}],"20":[{"n":4,"text":"And I saw thrones, and they sat on them, and judgment was committed to them. Then I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded for their witness to YahuShua and for the word of God, who had not worshiped the beast or his image, and had not received his mark on their foreheads or on their hands. And they lived and reigned with HaMashiach for a thousand years."},{"n":6,"text":"Blessed and holy is he who has part in the first resurrection. Over such the second death has no power, but they shall be priests of God and of HaMashiach, and shall reign with Him a thousand years."}],"22":[{"n":16,"text":"“I, YahuShua, have sent My angel to testify to you these things in the churches. I am the Root and the Offspring of David, the Bright and Morning Star.”"},{"n":20,"text":"He who testifies to these things says, “Surely I am coming quickly.” Amen. Even so, come, Lord YahuShua!"},{"n":21,"text":"The grace of our Lord YahuShua HaMashiach be with you all. Amen."}]}
};
